am-.html', 'snippet': 'The underfunded program encourages development in flood-prone areas.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It was clear long before Hurricane Harvey slammed into Texas that the National Flood Insurance Program, the government’s most important means of recovering from such disasters, needed to be overhauled. It fails to account for the full extent of flood risk, encourages development in areas known to be flood-prone and is not realistically funded.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/01/opinion/01fri1/01fri1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/09/01/opinion/01fri1/01fri1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/01/opinion/01fri1/01fri1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/01/opinion/01fri1/01fri1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 422, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/09/01/opinion/01fri1/01fri1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 422}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/01/opinion/01fri1/01fri1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 721, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/01/opinion/01fri1/01fri1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1441, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'How Federal Flood Insurance Puts Homes at Risk', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Holes in Flood Insurance', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Flood Insurance', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Flood Insurance Program', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Emergency Management Agency', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-09-01T01:53:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/f30e4ca2-ef5b-5c5d-a6a6-fe077ff562f6', 'word_count': 642, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f30e4ca2-ef5b-5c5d-a6a6-fe077ff562f6'}, {'abstract': 'A Patrick Berry Friday is a very good Friday indeed.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/08/31/crosswords/daily-puzzle-2017-09-01.html', 'snippet': 'A Patrick Berry Friday is a very good Friday indeed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FRIDAY PUZZLE — Don’t tell anyone, but this is a rough week for me. I took The Boy to college for his first semester, and I’m incredibly proud of how much he’s grown up in the past few years. I love the young man he’s become. He’s outgrown whatever teenage quirks he had, and he’s really nice to be around. And now he’s leaving. By the way, today’s puzzle is a really nice one by Patrick Berry.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/01/crosswords/01wordplay-monkey-bars/01wordplay-monkey-bars-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/09/01/crosswords/01wordplay