 she said.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/10/travel/Deals1/10italy1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/09/10/travel/Deals1/10italy1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/10/travel/Deals1/10italy1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/10/travel/Deals1/10italy1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/09/10/travel/Deals1/10italy1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/10/travel/Deals1/10italy1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/10/travel/Deals1/10italy1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Fall in Italy: Lovely Weather, Lower Prices', 'kicker': 'Chasing the Deal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Enjoying Fall in Italy', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hotels and Travel Lodgings', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AIRLINES AND AIRPLANES', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Italy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Sicily (Italy)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Lake Como (Italy)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Rome (Italy)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Amalfi Coast (Italy)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-09-01T09:00:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Shivani Vora', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Shivani', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vora', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/99c4cad9-3ac5-55f0-91bc-83f3d517a622', 'word_count': 409, 'uri': 'nyt://article/99c4cad9-3ac5-55f0-91bc-83f3d517a622'}, {'abstract': 'This week’s crime novels delve into the Spanish past and into film history, then grapple with two present-day children tormented by dangerous visions.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/09/01/books/review/crime-louise-penny-glass-houses.html', 'snippet': 'This week’s crime novels delve into the Spanish past and into film history, then grapple with two present-day children tormented by dangerous visions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Louise Penny wrote the book on escapist mysteries — a dozen of them, in fact, almost all set in the sheltered Canadian village of Three Pines. “It was a haven, a buffer, from the cares and cruelty of the world,” she tells us in GLASS HOUSES (Minotaur, $28.99), a place seemingly so free of malice and discord that Armand Gamache, chief superintendent of the Sûreté du Québec, and his wife, Reine-Marie, have made it their sanctuary. One of the pleasures of returning to this series is visiting old friends in the village like Gabri and Olivier, who run the convivial B&B; the artist Clara Morrow, whose startling portraits will haunt you; and (a personal favorite) Ruth Zardo, a poet who accurately describes herself as “a crazy old woman who prays for Satan and has a duck.”', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/03/books/review/0903-BKS-Crime/0903-BKS-Crime-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/09/03/books/review/0903-BKS-Crime/0903-BKS-Crime-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/03/books/review/0903-BKS-Crime/0903-BKS-Crime-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/03/books/review/0903-BKS-Crime/0903-BKS-Crime-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 907, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/09/03/books/review/0903-BKS-Crime/0903-BKS-Crime-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 907}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/03/books/review/0903-BKS-Crime/0903-BKS-Crime-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 678, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/03/books/review/0903-BKS-Crime/0903-BKS-Crime-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1355, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Mythic Revenge, a Mythic Film and Possibly Mythic Memories', 'kicker': 'Crime', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Modern-Day Black Death', 