ged homes, others remained in the grip of the crisis on Friday, cut off by still-rising floodwaters and living without running water for a second day.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Floodwaters Inundate Beaumont as Houston Assesses Damage', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Houston Goes Home to Find Vast Damage', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hurricane Harvey (2017)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Floods', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Houston (Tex)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Beaumont (Tex)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Harris County (Tex)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-09-01T09:00:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Audra D. S. Burch, Richard Pérez-Peña and Julie Turkewitz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Audra', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/53b97f11-e6d2-5781-877f-8a7f2a8f5a15', 'word_count': 1421, 'uri': 'nyt://article/53b97f11-e6d2-5781-877f-8a7f2a8f5a15'}, {'abstract': 'Americans are still divided over the legacy of the Vietnam War. Can Ken Burns and Lynn Novick’s 18-hour documentary help put the demons of that era — and of our own — to rest?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/09/01/arts/television/ken-burns-and-lynn-novick-tackle-the-vietnam-war.html', 'snippet': 'Americans are still divided over the legacy of the Vietnam War. Can Ken Burns and Lynn Novick’s 18-hour documentary help put the demons of that era — and of our own — to rest?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ken Burns shot to fame in 1990 with “The Civil War,” which drew record audiences for PBS and jump-started a revival of popular interest in the subject. Nearly three decades and more than 20 documentaries later, he is perhaps the nation’s most trusted historical brand, as much an icon of American-ness as baseball (the subject of his nine-part 1994 documentary) and apple pie (one of the few classic American themes he hasn’t taken on).', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/03/arts/03VIETNAM/03VIETNAM-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/09/03/arts/03VIETNAM/03VIETNAM-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/03/arts/03VIETNAM/03VIETNAM-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/03/arts/03VIETNAM/03VIETNAM-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 408, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/09/03/arts/03VIETNAM/03VIETNAM-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 408}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/03/arts/03VIETNAM/03VIETNAM-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 697, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/03/arts/03VIETNAM/03VIETNAM-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1393, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'sup