pe_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/50ebd5be-5515-59a8-92e1-98fc5c365e2b', 'word_count': 461, 'uri': 'nyt://article/50ebd5be-5515-59a8-92e1-98fc5c365e2b'}, {'abstract': 'It’s a big city, with plenty to do, see, hear and watch. Here’s a sampling of cultural highlights this weekend and over the week ahead.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/09/01/arts/things-to-do-in-nyc-great-comet-2-chainz.html', 'snippet': 'It’s a big city, with plenty to do, see, hear and watch. Here’s a sampling of cultural highlights this weekend and over the week ahead.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The latest side project from the popular American Ballet Theater principal dancer Daniil Simkin involves real-time motion sensors; costumes by Dior; and projections by his father, Dmitrij, also an accomplished ballet dancer. A commission by the Works & Process Rotunda Project, this 30-minute work — scheduled to be performed twice nightly, at 8 and 9:30 p.m., on Monday and Tuesday — features Mr. Simkin, the Ballet Theater soloist Cassandra Trenary, the Hubbard Street dancer Ana Lopez and Brett Conway in juicy choreography by the Hubbard Street house choreographer, Alejandro Cerrudo. With observers watching from above, standing along the Guggenheim’s spiraling ramps, the dancers will tangle with each other and their own shadows, which, thanks to technology, will seem to have developed minds of their own. BRIAN SCHAEFER', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/01/arts/01listdance/01listdance-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/09/01/arts/01listdance/01listdance-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/01/arts/01listdance/01listdance-thumb