ho faced each other in an epic at-bat in Game 7 of the Indians-Cubs showdown, are now with the Red Sox and the Yankees.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Jordan Michael Davis, the 2-year-old son of Rajai Davis, is not minding his p’s and q’s at the dinner table, his father knows a sure way to get his attention.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/04/sports/04YANKS-FEATURE1/04YANKS-FEATURE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/09/04/sports/04YANKS-FEATURE1/04YANKS-FEATURE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/04/sports/04YANKS-FEATURE1/04YANKS-FEATURE1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/04/sports/04YANKS-FEATURE1/04YANKS-FEATURE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 438, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/09/04/sports/04YANKS-FEATURE1/04YANKS-FEATURE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 438}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/04/sports/04YANKS-FEATURE1/04YANKS-FEATURE1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 748, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/04/sports/04YANKS-FEATURE1/04YANKS-FEATURE1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1496, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Actors in a World Series Drama Are Now Gracing a New Stage', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Actors in Drama At World Series Grace New Stage', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Davis, Rajai', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chapman, Aroldis (1988- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chicago Cubs', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cleveland Indians', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Boston Red Sox', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-09-03T20:58:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Billy Witz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Billy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Witz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/38a1cbbc-2477-58b9-a1c2-331222da7d1d', 'word_count': 1013, 'uri': 'nyt://article/38a1cbbc-2477-58b9-a1c2-331222da7d1d'}, {'abstract': 'In Stephen Baxter’s authorized follow-up to H. G. Wells’s science-fiction classic, the Martians return, and this time they know what they’re doing.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/09/03/books/massacre-of-mankind-sequel-to-war-of-worlds-stephen-baxter.html', 'snippet': 'In Stephen Baxter’s authorized follow-up to H. G. Wells’s science-fiction classic, the Martians return, and this time they know what they’re doing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It was 120 years ago that H. G. Wells’s “The War of the Worlds,” about a Martian invasion of Earth, appeared as a magazine serial. (In the United States, the story was rolled out in Cosmopolitan.) Nearly 80 years ago, a radio dramatization of the novel caused “a wave of mass hysteria,” according to The New York Times, among some listeners who didn’t know the terrifying scenario was fiction. Now, Stephen Baxter has written a sequel, “The Massacre of Mankind,” authorized by Wells’s estate. (Baxter is the author of dozens of science-fiction books, and, even more pertinently, a vice president of the H.G. Wells Society.) His book was published in Britain earlier this year, where The Guardian said: “It’s Baxter’s best novel in a long time, and this may be because it reads like a genuine labor of love.” Below, Baxter talks about the evolution of Wells’s original story, his own childhood love of science fiction and more.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/04/books/04baxter1/04baxter1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/09/04/books/04baxter1/04baxter1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/04/books/04baxter1/04baxter1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/04/books/04baxter1/04baxter1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 842, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/09/04/books/04baxter1/04baxter1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 842}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/04/books/04baxter1/04baxter1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 730, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legac