ontrol.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/09/04/arts/design/director-metropolitan-museum-search-daniel-weiss.html', 'snippet': 'The museum is searching for a director. Maybe it’s time for a woman to assume control.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There are many exciting museum shows to see across the country in coming months. But of particular interest to me will be the one unfolding in real time at the Metropolitan Museum of Art as this august institution tries to right itself after several years of staff unrest, financial mismanagement and overreach. A lot has happened since Thomas P. Campbell, its director of eight years, resigned under pressure in late February, but it’s not over. The most obvious questions are: Who will be the next director, and when will he — or, better yet, she — be appointed?', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '90', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/10/arts/10SMITH1/02metbreuer-desk-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/09/10/arts/10SMITH1/02metbreuer-desk-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/10/arts/10SMITH1/02metbreuer-desk-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/10/arts/10SMITH1/02metbreuer-desk-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/09/10/arts/10SMITH1/02metbreuer-desk-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/10/arts/10SMITH1/02metbreuer-desk-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/10/arts/10SMITH1/02metbreuer-desk-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Fall’s Most Fascinating Art Show? The Met Trying to Fix Itself', 'kicker': "Critic's Notebook", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Met Itself Is the Most Fascinating Show', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Metropolitan Museum of Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Weiss, Daniel H', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'de Montebello, Philippe', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Campbell, Thomas P', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-09-04T13:00:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roberta Smith', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roberta', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Smith', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4ab35e73-5974-537d-8eba-2cf1c14b242f', 'word_count': 1666, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4ab35e73-5974-537d-8eba-2cf1c14b242f'}, {'abstract': 'Does it even matter that so many questions were left unanswered?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/09/04/arts/television/twin-peaks-season-3-finale-recap.html', 'snippet': 'Does it even matter that so many questions were left unanswered?', 'lead_paragraph': 'In May of 1990, ABC aired the “Twin Peaks” Season 1 finale, and frustrated viewers who’d expected the show’s creators David Lynch and Mark Frost to resolve the “Who killed Laura Palmer?” mystery. In June of 1991, “Twin Peaks” Season 2 also ended with more questions than answers, and stuck fans with a cruel twist, revealing that heroic FBI Agent Dale Cooper had been replaced by an evil twin. So if you were confounded by the way the third (and perhaps last-ever) “Twin Peaks” season wrapped up last night ... well, call it tradition. Whether by circumstance or intent, this has always been a TV drama that eschews tidy resolutions.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/04/arts/television/04peaks-recap/04peaks-recap-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/09/04/arts/television/04peaks-recap/04peaks-recap-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/04/arts/television/04peaks-recap/04peaks-recap-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/04/arts/television/04peaks-recap/04peaks-recap-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/09/04/arts/television/04peaks-recap/04peaks-recap-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/04/arts/television/04peaks-recap/04peaks-recap-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/04/arts/television/04peaks-recap/04p