T07:21:01+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Opinion', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Editorials', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/f376437c-20d5-544c-bfc2-b4820328b135', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/f376437c-20d5-544c-bfc2-b4820328b135'}, {'abstract': 'With President Trump and Congress turning to tax policy, it’s worth revisiting a story about wealth from another era.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/09/05/opinion/rich-getting-richer-taxes.html', 'snippet': 'With President Trump and Congress turning to tax policy, it’s worth revisiting a story about wealth from another era.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A half-century ago, a top automobile executive named George Romney — yes, Mitt’s father — turned down several big annual bonuses. He did so, he told his company’s board, because he believed that no executive should make more than $225,000 a year (which translates into almost $2 million today).', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/05/opinion/05leonhardtWeb/05leonhardtWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/09/05/opinion/05leonhardtWeb/05leonhardtWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/05/opinion/05leonhardtWeb/05leonhardtWeb-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/05/opinion/05leonhardtWeb/05leonhardtWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 427, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/09/05/opinion/05leonhardtWeb/05leonhardtWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 427}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/05/opinion/05leonhardtWeb/05leonhardtWeb-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 729, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/05/opinion/05leonhardtWeb/05leonhardtWeb-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1459, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'When the Rich Said No to Getting Richer', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Columnist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'When the Rich  Said No to Getting Richer', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Executive Compensation', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Taxes (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'High Net Worth Individuals', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Income Inequality', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, George W', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-09-05T07:21:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Leonhardt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Leonhardt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/534ab5fc-c73b-566c-95aa-5d57a8266d16', 'word_count': 849, 'uri': 'nyt://article/534ab5fc-c73b-566c-95aa-5d57a8266d16'}, {'abstract': 'Whether her message can resonate is in question. But we’re pleased that she is prepared to give her Democratic opponent a lively challenge.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/09/05/opinion/endorsement-nicole-malliotakis-mayor.html', 'snippet': 'Whether her message can resonate is in question. But we’re pleased that she is prepared to give her Democratic opponent a lively challenge.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As the daughter of a father from Crete (and of a Cuban-born mother), Nicole Malliotakis may be familiar with the Greek myth of Sisyphus, doomed for eternity to push a boulder up a hill, only to have it roll back on him every time. Running as a Republican for citywide office in New York is kind of like that — only maybe more frustrating.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/05/opinion/05tue2web/05tue2web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/09/05/opinion/05tue2web/05tue2web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/05/opinion/05tue2web/05tue2web-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/05/opinion/05tue2web/05tue2web-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/09/05/opinion/05tue2web/05tue2web-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/05/opinion/05tue2web/05tue2web-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/05/opinion/05tue2web/05tue2web-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Nicole Malliotakis, a Gutsy G.O.P. Challenger', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Nicole Malliotakis, a Gutsy G.O.P. Challenger', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Malliotakis, Nicole', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'de Blasio, Bill', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections, Mayors', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-09-05T07:21:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/44d977ea-3685-5040-8a20-566eed9722ec', 'word_count': 324, 'uri': 'nyt://article/44d977ea-3685-5040-8a20-566eed9722ec'}, {'abstract': 'Forty years ago, we sent two Voyager spacecraft into the cosmos. Will we continue our own journey of discovery?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/09/05/opinion/pondering-voyagers-interstellar-journeys-and-our-own.html', 'snippet': 'Forty years ago, we sent two Voyager spacecraft into the cosmos. Will we continue our own journey of discovery?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Tempe, Ariz. — Tuesday is the 40th anniversary of the launch of Voyager 1, which, paradoxically, was shot into space two weeks after its partner spacecraft, Voyager 2. With all of the turbulent terrestrial news of late, it may seem like humanity is stuck in the past, dominated by religious wars and racial violence. But pondering the journey of these two small space explorers reminds us of just how far humanity has traveled in just a few decades.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/05/opinion/05krauss/05krauss-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/09/05/opinion/05krauss/05krauss-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/05/opinion/05krauss/05krauss-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/05/opinion/05krauss/05krauss-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 337, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/09/05/opinion/05krauss/05krauss-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 337}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/05/opinion/05krauss/05krauss-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/05/opinion/05krauss/05krauss-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1152, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Pondering Voyagers’ Interstellar Journeys, and Our Own', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Voyages of Discovery', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Voyager Project', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Space and Astronomy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-09-05T07:21:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lawrence M. Krauss', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lawrence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/dc76d932-cfa3-520b-878c-3652a009b346', 'word_count': 914, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dc76d932-cfa3-520b-878c-3652a009b346'}, {'abstract': 'Afghans who risked their lives working for the U.S. military were granted safe haven in California. Danger awaited them there as well.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2017/09/05/they-worked-for-america-now-these-afghans-face-violence-and-poverty-here/', 'snippet': 'Afghans who risked their lives working for the U.S. military were granted safe haven in California. Danger awaited them there as well.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PERPIGNAN, France — Mustafa Rafi, an Afghan electrical engineer, risked his life working with the U.S. military in his homeland. Because he faced a grave threat from the Taliban, he and his family were relocated to Sacramento in June 2015 thanks to a special immigrant visa. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'They Worked for America. Now These Afghans Face Violence and Poverty Here.', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value':