tempted Murders and Homicides', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organized Crime', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bars and Nightclubs', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Little Italy (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Mulberry Street Bar (Manhattan, NY, Bar)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-09-06T09:00:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Wilson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wilson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/eebffddd-93e0-5d1e-a3c9-b069ecbfed6a', 'word_count': 1069, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eebffddd-93e0-5d1e-a3c9-b069ecbfed6a'}, {'abstract': 'With “Junk,” the Pulitzer-winning playwright Ayad Akhtar examines financial chicanery in the 1980s — and how it shaped the blind worship of affluence today.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/09/06/theater/taking-on-wall-streets-church-of-big-money.html', 'snippet': 'With “Junk,” the Pulitzer-winning playwright Ayad Akhtar examines financial chicanery in the 1980s — and how it shaped the blind worship of affluence today.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At the age of 7, Ayad Akhtar, the son of two doctors in suburban Milwaukee, was seized by a religious fervor. He began asking his parents to take him to the one mosque in the area, a converted schoolhouse on the city’s Polish south side that they only occasionally attended. He taught himself to pray, and he saw the Prophet Muhammad in his dreams. One year, on the day in the calendar when some Muslims say all of creation bowed in respect to Muhammad, he stayed up all night, looking out his bedroom window and waiting to see the trees bend. “I don’t know why, but I was a very sensitive kid. I had an acute awareness of splendor,” Mr. Akhtar told me in one of the conversations we had over the summer. “The only thing that really responded to that register of life for me was the Quran — and ‘Star Wars.’”', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/10/arts/10AKHTAR/10AKHTAR-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/09/10/arts/10AKHTAR/10AKHTAR-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/10/arts/10AKHTAR/10AKHTAR-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/10/arts/10AKHTAR/10AKHTAR-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 750, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/09/10/arts/10AKHTAR/10AKHTAR-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 750}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/10/arts/10AKHTAR/10AKHTAR-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 820, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/10/arts/10AKHTAR/10AKHTAR-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1639, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Plunging His Pen Into the Dark Heart of 1980s Wall Street', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Following the Money', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Muslim Americans', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'AKHTAR, AYAD', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Junk (Play)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'La Jolla Playhouse', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lincoln Center for the Performing Arts', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'American Dervish (Book)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-09-06T09:00:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Sokolove', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sokolove', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7d9c392c-fcf4-5485-9782-83108f6965ee', 'word_count': 3428, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7d9c392c-fcf4-5485-9782-83108f6965ee'}, {'abstract': "As Harvey's rains bore down on Texas, a 911 dispatcher and a pastor's daughter felt nature at its fiercest — and saw humanity at its best.", 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/us/100000005408538/harvey-storm.html', 'snippet': "As Harvey's rains bore down on Texas, a 911 dispatcher and a pastor's daughter felt nature at its fiercest — and saw humanity at its best.", 'lead_paragraph': "As Harvey's rains bore down on Texas, a 911 dispatcher and a pastor's daughter felt nature at its fiercest — and saw humanity at its best.", 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/06/multimedia/final-truck/final-truck-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 409, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge':