eight': 608, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/07/insider/06-sid-01/06-sid-01-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1216, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Indian Jewelry: A History Lesson', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jewels and Jewelry', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-09-06T17:51:26+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'subsection_name': 'Fashion & Beauty', 'byline': {'original': 'By Barbara Anastacio', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Barbara', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Anastacio', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/cfb2d4f6-796d-52ac-b8c8-0f356a8ee9c7', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/cfb2d4f6-796d-52ac-b8c8-0f356a8ee9c7'}, {'abstract': 'An heir to the Gem Palace, Jaipur’s legendary jewelry emporium, shares his inspirations — and vision.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/09/06/t-magazine/fashion/sid-kasliwal-gem-palace-profile-in-style.html', 'snippet': 'An heir to the Gem Palace, Jaipur’s legendary jewelry emporium, shares his inspirations — and vision.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As a boy, Siddharth Kasliwal accompanied his father, Munnu — an heir to the Gem Palace, Jaipur’s legendary jewelry emporium — to mines in Brazil and on business trips to Paris. ‘‘He would give me ruby and sapphire beads to occupy me,’’ the younger Kasliwal says, ‘‘as though they were toys.’’ In the jewelry trade for nine generations, the Kasliwals and their storied 109-year-old store and workshop have created spectacular pieces for royals (Princess Diana), maharanis (the Ava Gardner-like Gayatri Devi of Jaipur) and rock stars (Mick Jagger). In the wake of Munnu’s 2012 death at age 54 from brain cancer, his 33-year-old son, who friends call Sid, has emerged in his own right as a designer — and bon vivant. Munnu brought Indian fine jewelry the international recognition once reserved for European houses and championed previously unsung stones like the spinel; his son, who opened a vivid new Mumbai boutique in 2015, aims to further marry historical influences with contemporary settings in his work. Good-naturedly dodging his mother’s entreaties to settle down, the peripatetic and engaging Kasliwal scours the world for outrageous gems (a recent find was an old 10-carat mine diamond at a Las Vegas antiques show) and the best parties. When not on the road or in India, he can be found in his Upper East Side Manhattan atelier, entertaining clients in the scarlet-upholstered suite of a townhouse, surrounded by velvet-lined trays of glittering adornments. ‘‘I was raised for this,’’ he says. ‘‘It’s the best life you can imagine.’’', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '94', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/01/t-magazine/sid-kasliwal-slide-GD5B/sid-kasliwal-slide-GD5B-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/09/01/t-magazine/sid-kasliwal-slide-GD5B/sid-kasliwal-slide-GD5B-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/01/t-magazine/sid-kasliwal-slide-GD5B/sid-kasliwal-slide-GD5B-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/01/t-magazi