ank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Abel, Pilar', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Spain', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-09-06T18:02:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Raphael Minder', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Raphael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Minder', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a5a1d8ce-454a-5182-9e79-e5879211ff81', 'word_count': 323, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a5a1d8ce-454a-5182-9e79-e5879211ff81'}, {'abstract': 'Ben Blum tries to get to the bottom of his cousin’s participation in an armed bank robbery.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/09/06/books/review-ranger-games-ben-blum.html', 'snippet': 'Ben Blum tries to get to the bottom of his cousin’s participation in an armed bank robbery.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To a hammer, everything looks like a nail. To an Army Ranger — or to some Rangers, it seems fair to say — every building looks like a potential target. In 2006, Pfc. Alex Blum would often find himself sitting with his Ranger buddies near their base in Tacoma, Wash., imagining the logistics of taking down local establishments. Especially enthusiastic about these exercises was Specialist Luke Elliott Sommer, a more senior Ranger with two combat tours behind him. He turned every brief, banal excursion — to Dairy Queen, Quiznos, a porn shop — into a teachable moment.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/07/books/07bookblum2/07bookblum2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/09/07/books/07bookblum2/07bookblum2-thumbStandard.jpg', 't