photographer Glen Luchford has shot hundreds of fashion images over his more than two-decade- career. In 1991, he met Jack Webb and hired him as a lighting assistant. Webb, a photographer in his own right, began to stand in for models on set — so that Luchford could test the lighting. As the writer Lou Stoppard writes in the book, “Those pictures were made without the sense that they’d ever been seen again, because usually what happens at the end of a session is you separate test shots out and they get trashed,” Luchford says in a conversation with Webb that is included in his new book, “The Agony and the Ecstasy: Jack Webb by Glen Luchford,” which will be published by IDEA this week. “But for some reason, I hung onto them.”', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'One Lighting Assistant, Captured in Photos Over Two Decades', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Photography; Shadow Images', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-09-06T22:39:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'subsection_name': 'Art', 'byline': {'original': 'By Isabel Wilkinson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Isabel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wilkinson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b95bb10c-a14a-5f1a-a6a6-d94c1ddf9fd6', 'word_count': 240, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b95bb10c-a14a-5f1a-a6a6-d94c1ddf9fd6'}, {'abstract': 'The Styles desk and T Magazine begin preparing for the twice-yearly event months in advance.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/09/06/insider/fashion-week-month-reporting.html', 'snippet': 'The Styles desk and T Magazine begin preparing for the twice-yearly event months in advance.', 'lead_paragrap