ports/baseball/minnesota-twins-playoffs.html', 'snippet': 'No team has ever lost 100 games one season and reached the playoffs the next. But the Twins believe they can do it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ST. PETERSBURG, Fla. — As the home runs piled up late last season for the Minnesota Twins’ Brian Dozier, so did a gnawing sense of emptiness. Dozier set an American League record for homers by a second baseman, with 40 of his 42 coming at the position. But his team stumbled to 103 losses, a low point across more than five decades in Minnesota. Baseball was no fun.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/07/sports/07kepner/07kepner-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/09/07/sports/07kepner/07kepner-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/07/sports/07kepner/07kepner-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/07/sports/07kepner/07kepner-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 381, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/09/07/sports/07kepner/07kepner-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 381}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/07/sports/07kepner/07kepner-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 651, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/07/sports/07kepner/07