icle/833f2d45-85bf-5419-88e2-1a5e92c9d989'}, {'abstract': 'Manager Joe Girardi, who is famously tight-lipped about reliever roles, came as close as he ever has to making a definitive statement on his closer.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/09/06/sports/baseball/aroldis-chapman-yankees.html', 'snippet': 'Manager Joe Girardi, who is famously tight-lipped about reliever roles, came as close as he ever has to making a definitive statement on his closer.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BALTIMORE — For nearly two decades, there was never a question about who would close out a Yankees game. From 1997 to 2013 — with a detour because of a serious knee injury in 2012 — it was Mariano Rivera. Others then followed — David Robertson, Andrew Miller, Aroldis Chapman and sometimes Dellin Betances. Starting this season, the Yankees thought, it would be Chapman again for the next five years.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/07/sports/07yankees/07yankees-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/09/07/sports/07yankees/07yankees-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/07/sports/07yankees/07yankees-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/07/sports/07yankees/07yankees-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 525, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/09/07/sports/07yankees/07yankees-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 525}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo