eported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/19eb5d98-33f9-5533-b16a-70d87ffa7c3a', 'word_count': 641, 'uri': 'nyt://article/19eb5d98-33f9-5533-b16a-70d87ffa7c3a'}, {'abstract': 'New York Fashion Week begins with a history lesson. And it’s a surprising amount of fun.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/09/07/fashion/tom-ford-narciso-rodriguez-new-york-spring-2018.html', 'snippet': 'New York Fashion Week begins with a history lesson. And it’s a surprising amount of fun.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The 1990s have been resurgent of late, largely thanks to their somewhat ignoble contributions to contemporary life: reality television and “Baywatch”; White House scandal and congressional shutdown; and, of course, the introduction of Donald J. Trump as a pop culture tabloid star. Well, we all need something to blame. Why not a time period?', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/07/fashion/07review-ford-1sub/07review-ford-1sub-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/09/07/fashion/07review-ford-1sub/07review-ford-1sub-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/07/fashion/07review-ford-1sub/07review-ford-1sub-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/07/fashion/07review-ford-1sub/07review-ford-1sub-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/09/07/fashion/07re