', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/08/arts/08unknown1/08unknown1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/09/08/arts/08unknown1/08unknown1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/08/arts/08unknown1/08unknown1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/08/arts/08unknown1/08unknown1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/09/08/arts/08unknown1/08unknown1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/08/arts/08unknown1/08unknown1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/08/arts/08unknown1/08unknown1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1363, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: The Hard Road of Decency in ‘The Unknown Girl’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Hard Road Of Goodness', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Unknown Girl (Movie)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dardenne, Jean-Pierre', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dardenne, Luc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-09-07T14:29:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By A.O. Scott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'A.', 'middlename': 'O.', 'lastname': 'Scott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/514c95f3-5f3c-5bb4-92fe-d6c7d1101f51', 'word_count': 489, 'uri': 'nyt://article/514c95f3-5f3c-5bb4-92fe-d6c7d1101f51'}, {'abstract': 'Bill Nighy pursues a serial killer in 19th-century London in Juan Carlos Medina’s film.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/09/07/movies/the-limehouse-golem-review.html', 'snippet': 'Bill Nighy pursues a serial killer in 19th-century London in Juan Carlos Medina’s film.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Owner of a face that’s one of the marvels of modern cinema, Bill Nighy can give even the most somber movie a comic bent. So his central presence in “The Limehouse Golem,” a baroque Victorian whodunit set in London’s East End, is like a wink-wink signal that what we’re seeing is being played for laughs, not scares. Yet despite the lurid images and florid dialogue, this over-the-top adaptation of Peter Ackroyd’s 1994 novel takes itself very seriously indeed.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/08/arts/08LIMEHOUSE1/08LIMEHOUSE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/09/08/arts/08LIMEHOUSE1/08LIMEHOUSE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/08/arts/08LIMEHOUSE1/08LIMEHOUSE1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/08/arts/08LIMEHOUSE1/08LIMEHOUSE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/09/08/arts/08LIMEHOUSE1/08LIMEHOUSE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/08/arts/08LIMEHOUSE1/08LIMEHOUSE1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 577, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/08/arts/08LIMEHOUSE1/08LIMEHOUSE1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1153, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: In ‘The Limehouse Golem,’ <strong></strong>Bawdy Limericks and Bloody Corpses', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Limehouse Golem', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Limehouse Golem (Movie)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Medina, Juan Carlos', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nighy, Bill', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Booth, Douglas', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ACKROYD, PETER', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-09-07T14:31:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeannette Catsoulis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeannette', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Catsoulis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/11a45760-643b-5390-a7f0-fa3f5f1eba8d', 'word_count': 244, 'uri': 'nyt://article/11a45760-643b-5390-a7f0-fa3f5f1eba8d'}, {'abstract': 'This thoughtful documentary raises tough questions about big-game hunting and wildlife conservation.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/09/07/movies/trophy-review.html', 'snippet': 'This thoughtful documentary raises tough questions about big-game hunting and wildlife conservation.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Trophy,” an extraordinary documentary from Shaul Schwarz and Christina Clusiau, is filled with astonishing sights. An American hunter welling up over the body of the lion he has just shot; a South African rhino breeder calmly sawing the horns off his helpless charges. The intimacy of the film’s images and the surprising candor of its participants are disarming: Whatever your initial response, be prepared to re-evaluate.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/08/arts/08trophy/08trophy-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/09/08/arts/08trophy/08trophy-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/08/arts/08trophy/08trophy-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/08/arts/08trophy/08trophy-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 314, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/09/08/arts/08trophy/08trophy-articleLarge.jpg', '