adca'}, {'abstract': 'When the great hurricane walloped Galveston 117 years ago, The New York Times was helpless. Hurricane Harvey posed its own challenges.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/09/07/insider/the-times-and-texas-hurricanes.html', 'snippet': 'When the great hurricane walloped Galveston 117 years ago, The New York Times was helpless. Hurricane Harvey posed its own challenges.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Not a wire is working into Galveston, either telegraph or telephone, and as all bridges carried wires, the fears that all these structures are gone is strengthened,” The New York Times reported ominously on Sept. 9, 1900, a day after Galveston Island on the Gulf of Mexico was pummeled by what remains the deadliest hurricane in national history.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/07/insider/07insider-galveston-a/07insider-galveston-a-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/09/07/insider/07insider-galveston-a/07insider-galveston-a-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/07/insider/07insider-galveston-a/07insider-galveston-a-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/07/insider/07insider-galveston-a/07insider-galveston-a-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 337, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/09/07/insider/07insider-galveston-a/07insider-galveston-a-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 337}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': '