ename': None, 'lastname': 'Casey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Susan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Abad', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3d457e37-7e09-57f1-b0ca-d8b5fb6b50f6', 'word_count': 729, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3d457e37-7e09-57f1-b0ca-d8b5fb6b50f6'}, {'abstract': 'A documentary captures the routines of an Irish boarding school and two of its cherished teachers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/09/07/movies/review-school-life-neasa-ni-chianain-and-david-rane.html', 'snippet': 'A documentary captures the routines of an Irish boarding school and two of its cherished teachers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'John and Amanda Leyden have taught at Headfort School in Kells, Ireland, for so long than the headmaster, Dermot Dix, recognizes at one point that Ms. Leyden is using the same children’s novel that she taught his class many years ago. Neasa Ni Chianain and David Rane’s documentary “School Life” is a loving portrait, primarily, of the inspirational educator couple, who command the respect of their students and always seem to know what a particular child needs to hear.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/08/arts/08schoollife2/08schoollife2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/09/08/arts/08schoollife2/08schoollife2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/08/arts/08schoollife2/08schoollife2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_na