', '_id': 'nyt://article/dada8ff1-b11f-573a-9921-a43ed7e4ba1c', 'word_count': 190, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dada8ff1-b11f-573a-9921-a43ed7e4ba1c'}, {'abstract': 'Elisabeth Moss returns for Season 2 of the Jane Campion crime series.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/09/07/arts/television/top-of-the-lake-china-girl-tv-review.html', 'snippet': 'Elisabeth Moss returns for Season 2 of the Jane Campion crime series.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Elisabeth Moss is a vessel for cultural misogyny. Her TV characters have been harassed, sexually assaulted, threatened, degraded, lied to and betrayed. How much sexist abuse can befall one person? Oh, plenty. Between “Mad Men,” in which she played the ambitious but put-upon Peggy Olsen; “Top of the Lake,” in which she plays sex-crimes detective Robin Griffin; and “The Handmaid’s Tale,” in which she plays the enslaved Offred, one can watch Ms. Moss survive sexist torture in stories set in the past, the present and the crypto future.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/08/arts/08LAKEjp2/08LAKEjp2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/09/08/arts/08LAKEjp2/08LAKEjp2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/08/arts/08LAKEjp2/08LAKEjp2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/08/arts/08LAKEjp2/08LAKEjp2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/09/08/arts/08LAKEjp2/08LAKEjp2-articleLa