ted for 1.1 million students at New York City public schools on Thursday. For many, that meant managing first-day jitters and meeting old, and new, friends.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/09/07/nyregion/new-backpacks-and-beginnings.html', 'snippet': 'The new school year started for 1.1 million students at New York City public schools on Thursday. For many, that meant managing first-day jitters and meeting old, and new, friends.', 'lead_paragraph': 'New pencils (do they still use pencils?), bright backpacks (they still have those) and first-day jitters: Back to school is upon us. For the little ones entering classrooms for the first time, there may be tears. But for the veterans like middle schoolers and high school teens, there is stoicism. Crisp in uniforms or clad in trendy clothes — a sort of schoolyard armor — they stride out of summer and over zebra street crossings with purpose, catching up with old friends, and perhaps, for a secret second, grasping a parent’s hand. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/08/nyregion/08firstday1/08firstday1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/09/08/nyregion/08firstday1/08firstday1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/08/nyregion/08firstday1/08firstday1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/08/nyregion/08firstday1/08firstday1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge':