e, which struck off the Pacific Coast, set off tsunami warnings and scattered frightened residents into the streets as far as Mexico City.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/09/08/world/americas/mexico-earthquake.html', 'snippet': 'The quake, which struck off the Pacific Coast, set off tsunami warnings and scattered frightened residents into the streets as far as Mexico City.', 'lead_paragraph': 'JUCHITÁN DE ZARAGOZA, Mexico — Thousands of homes in this city were severely damaged. Half of the 19th-century city hall, with its 30 arches, collapsed. The main hospital here was so devastated that staff members evacuated patients to an empty lot and worked by the light of their cellphones.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mexico Earthquake, Strongest in a Century, Kills Dozens', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Strongest Quake to Shake Mexico in a Century Leaves Dozens Dead', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Chiapas, Mexico, Earthquake (September 7, 2017)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mexico', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Earthquakes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tidal Waves and Tsunamis', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mexico City (Mexico)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chiapas (Mexico)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-09-08T05:17:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paulina Villegas, Elisabeth Malkin and Kirk Semple', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paulina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Villegas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '',