ime East Village resident wakes early, avoids the brunch crowd, and looks for inspiration in books, trees, art shows and dance performances.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/09/08/nyregion/how-henry-threadgill-composer-spends-his-sundays.html', 'snippet': 'The longtime East Village resident wakes early, avoids the brunch crowd, and looks for inspiration in books, trees, art shows and dance performances.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For decades, Henry Threadgill, the Pulitzer Prize-winning musician and composer, has been racking up critical accolades, not to mention fans, with his jazz-influenced compositions. On Sept. 23, he will introduce a new work at Jazz at Lincoln Center: “Dirt, and More Dirt,” which was inspired by the longstanding conceptual-art piece in SoHo, the New York Earth Room. For most of his adult life, Mr. Threadgill, 73, has been a resident of the East Village, estimating that he has lived on almost every street in the neighborhood since moving there in 1975. He currently shares a two-bedroom apartment with his wife, Senti, an administrator at New York University, and his daughter, Nhumi, a college student.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/10/nyregion/10ROUTINE3/10ROUTINE3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/09/10/nyregion/10ROUTINE3/10ROUTINE3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/10/nyregion/10ROUTINE3/10ROUTINE3-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/10/nyregion/10ROUTINE3/10ROUTINE3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/09/10/nyregion/10ROUTINE3/10ROUTINE3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/10/nyregion/10ROUTINE3/10ROUTINE3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/10/nyregion/10ROUTINE3/10ROUTINE3-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'How Henry Threadgill, Composer, Spends His Sundays', 'kicker': 'Sunday Routine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Time for Music, Trees and Other Mysteries', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pulitzer Prizes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lincoln Center for the Performing Arts', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Threadgill, Henry', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'East Village (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-09-08T11:00:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metropolitan', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tammy La Gorce', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tammy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'La Gorce', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/efc2344b-2dd3-552c-8559-9eb587b0f318', 'word_count': 764, 'uri': 'nyt://article/efc2344b-2dd3-552c-8559-9eb587b0f318'}, {'abstract': 'Camps in Bangladesh, already crowded and underserved, are “b