bstract': 'The Civilian Complaint Review Board found that Officer Daniel Pantaleo used a chokehold and restricted Eric Garner’s breathing, a person familiar with the case said.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/09/08/nyregion/eric-garner-chokehold-review-board.html', 'snippet': 'The Civilian Complaint Review Board found that Officer Daniel Pantaleo used a chokehold and restricted Eric Garner’s breathing, a person familiar with the case said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A New York City agency that investigates police misconduct has found that the officer who put his arm around the neck of  Eric Garner before his death did use a chokehold and restricted Mr. Garner’s breathing, a person familiar with the case said on Friday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/09/nyregion/09garner/09garner-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/09/09/nyregion/09garner/09garner-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/09/nyregion/09garner/09garner-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/09/nyregion/09garner/09garner-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/09/09/nyregion/09garner/09garner-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/09/nyregion/09garner/09garner-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/09/nyregion/09garner/09garner-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Review Board Recommends Stiffest Punishment for Officer in Garner Case', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Review Board Finds Officer Used Chokehold on Garner', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Garner, Eric', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pantaleo, Daniel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police Brutality, Misconduct and Shootings', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil Rights and Liberties', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Civilian Complaint Review Board', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Staten Island (NYC)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-09-08T20:27:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Benjamin Mueller', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Benjamin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mueller', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6956448b-e56d-5200-8d48-42004f210a44', 'word_count': 823, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6956448b-e56d-5200-8d48-42004f210a44'}, {'abstract': "A not exhaustive list of what's on our radar.", 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/09/08/t-magazine/zaria-forman-eris-parfums-editors-picks.html', 'snippet': "A not exhaustive list of what's on our radar.", 'lead_paragraph': 'On a leafy block of Cypress Avenue, which runs parallel to the Los Angeles River in Northeast L.A.’s Cypress Park neighborhood, the writer and editor Christie Hayden has opened Oof Books. Hayden, who developed a love for artist-made books while a graduate student at the Maryland Institute College of Art and most recently worked with Hauser & Wirth’s Book & Printed Matter Lab, found the pocket-size space while searching for an apartment on Craigslist. The idea for a bookshop came together almost immediately. She tapped designers Jonathan Olivares, Paul Matevosyan and Raffy Mardirossian to create simple, bold shelving — painted mustard yellow in a nod to the Ed Ruscha painting from which the shop takes its name — and began sourcing books. Oof specializes in artist-made and locally published books and zines, as well as older catalogs and monographs. Some of Hayden’s favorite recent finds include Jenny Holzer’s “Truisms” and a Fernand Léger that she says, “I’m definitely going to grieve a bit to sell.” The shop also features art objects by ceramist Grant Levy-Lucero and hosts regular work and talks from emerging L.A. artists.  — MERRELL HAMBLETON ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/08/t-magazine/08tmag-tel-slide-FI17/08tmag-tel-slide-FI17-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/09/08/t-magazine/08tmag-tel-slide-FI17/08tmag-tel-slide-FI17-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/08/t-magazine/08tmag-tel-slide-FI17/08tmag-tel-slide-FI17-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/08/t-magazine/08tmag-tel-slide-FI17/08tmag-tel-slide-FI17-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'x