 magazine, taking over from Robert Silvers, who died in March after having edited it since 1963.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/09/09/books/ian-buruma-new-york-review-of-books-robert-silvers.html', 'snippet': 'Buruma has officially begun his tenure at the intellectual magazine, taking over from Robert Silvers, who died in March after having edited it since 1963.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Some shoes are harder to fill than others. Robert Silvers, the editor synonymous with The New York Review of Books, ran the left-leaning intellectual magazine with single-minded fervor from the time he co-founded it in 1963 until he died at 87 in March. His shoes may as well be Shaquille O’Neal’s.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/11/arts/11BURUMA/11BURUMA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/09/11/arts/11BURUMA/11BURUMA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/11/arts/11BURUMA/11BURUMA-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/11/arts/11BURUMA/11BURUMA-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 884, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/09/11/arts/11BURUMA/11BURUMA-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 884}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/11/arts/11BURUMA/11BURUMA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 695, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0