: {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/11/opinion/11blowWEB2/merlin-to-scoop-126270833-208832-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1392, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Soul Survival in Trump’s Hell', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Columnist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Soul Survival In Trump’s  Hell on Earth', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Voter Registration and Requirements', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Russian Interference in 2016 US Elections and Ties to Trump Associates', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-09-11T07:21:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Charles M. Blow', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Charles', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/e7d6b5c3-3c12-53c2-b1f8-51b18f53fb4d', 'word_count': 877, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e7d6b5c3-3c12-53c2-b1f8-51b18f53fb4d'}, {'abstract': 'We must emulate the families of terror victims who wouldn’t let their loved ones’ memory be erased.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/09/11/opinion/remembering-the-disappeared.html', 'snippet': 'We must emulate the families of terror victims who wouldn’t let their loved ones’ memory be erased.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DURHAM, N.C. — Of the 2,753 victims of the terrorist attack on the World Trade Center on Sept. 11, 2001, no physical trace has been found for 1,112 of them. Thus, for 40 percent of those who died that day, no remains have been returned to their families. In the aftermath of the carnage, some people exhibited photos, family snapshots, of those who had vanished and remained unaccounted for, despite the efforts of the authorities.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/11/opinion/11dorfman/11dorfman-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/09/11/opinion/11dorfman/11dorfman-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/11/opinion/11dorfman/11dorfman-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/11/opinion/11dorfman/11dorfman-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 608, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/09/11/opinion/11dorfman/11dorfman-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 608}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/11/opinion/11dorfman/11dorfman-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1011, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/11/opinion/11dorfman/11dorfman-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1650, 'width': 1629, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Remembering the Disappeared', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Remembering the Disappeared', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'September 11 (2001)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Human Rights and Human Rights Violations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': "Coups D'Etat and Attempted Coups D'Etat", 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chile', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-09-11T07:21:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ariel Dorfman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ariel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dorfman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/017a0e38-a71d-5164-91d4-8da6615e6964', 'word_count': 931, 'uri': 'nyt://article/017a0e38-a71d-5164-91d4-8da6615e6964'}, {'abstract': 'As a teacher who has had to jump through New York’s certification hoops, I’m pleased by a plan to let charter schools certify teachers themselves.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/09/11/opinion/teacher-certification-new-york.html', 'snippet': 'As a teacher who has had to jump through New York’s certification hoops, I’m pleased by a plan to let charter schools certify teachers themselves.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When schools reopened in New York last week, students were greeted by teachers who had spent the summer preparing for their return. Unfortunately, many of those teachers had had to devote some of their time not to lesson plans, but to a state teacher-certification process that emphasizes bureaucratic procedures more than real-world qualifications.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': '