idth': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/14/fashion/11SUIweb/11SUIweb-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1377, 'width': 1982, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Last Lost Flower Children of Anna Sui', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Flower Children Arrive, Long After the Hippies Have Left', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sui, Anna', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'New York Fashion Week', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-09-12T17:01:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Guy Trebay', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Guy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Trebay', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e816c136-feb5-5695-97ef-ba6ab75096b0', 'word_count': 507, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e816c136-feb5-5695-97ef-ba6ab75096b0'}, {'abstract': 'In his magnificent documentary, “Ex Libris: The New York Public Library,” Frederick Wiseman takes his camera into the halls where people read, learn and seek a perfect union.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/09/12/movies/ex-libris-new-york-public-library-review.html', 'snippet': 'In his magnificent documentary, “Ex Libris: The New York Public Library,” Frederick Wiseman takes his camera into the halls where people read, learn and seek a perfect union.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The main branch of the New York Public Library — the Beaux-Arts landmark at Fifth Avenue and 42 Street with the stone lions — opened its doors to a ravenous population on May 24, 1911. More than 50,000 souls are said to have flowed through its marble grandeur, inaugurating what has been an intimate, mutually sustaining union between the public and its library. In his magnificent new documentary “Ex Libris: The New York Public Library,” Frederick Wiseman takes his camera into those same halls as well as into more humble city branches. He sweeps into atriums and down corridors, pauses in reading and meeting rooms, and lays bare this complex, glorious organism that is the democratic ideal incarnate.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/13/arts/13exlibris3/13exlibris3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/09/13/arts/13exlibris3/13exlibris3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/13/arts/13exlibris3/13exlibris3-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/13/arts/13exlibris3/13exlibris3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/09/13/arts/13exlibris3/13exlibris3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/13/arts/13exlibris3/13exlibris3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/13/arts/13exlibris3/13exlibris3-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: We the (Library-Card Carrying) People of ‘Ex Libris’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Books and Souls,  Guarded by Lions', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Ex Libris: The New York Public Library (Movie)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Documentary Films and Programs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Public Library', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wiseman, Frederick', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Libraries and Librarians', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-09-12T17:10:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Manohla Dargis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Manohla', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dargis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/6b3e862f-b5ee-50df-8b2a-62e7441d1357', 'word_count': 1008, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6b3e862f-b5ee-50df-8b2a-62e7441d1357'}, {'abstract': 'The investigative journalists Michael Isikoff and David Corn will publish their new book, tentatively titled “The Russian Connection,” in March.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/09/12/books/new-book-will-investigate-trump-russia-connection.html', 'snippet': 'The investigative journalists Michael Isikoff and David Corn will publish their new book, tentatively titled “The Russian Connection,” in March.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Conspiracies surrounding Russian meddling in American politics used to be the terrain of novelists. Now nonfiction writers get to dig in. Hillary Clinton’s “What Happened,” her account of the 2016 presidential election, went on sale Tuesday, and another book about the election, an investigative look by two journalists into the controversies surrounding Donald J. Trump, Vladimir Putin and Russia’s influence, isn’t far behind.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New Book Will Investigate Trump-Russia Connection', 'kicker': 'Books News', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Book to Examine Trump-Russia Ties', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Isikoff, Michael', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Corn, David', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Russian Interference in 2016 US Elections and Ties to Trump Associates', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Book Trade and Publishing', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-09-12T17:29:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Williams', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Williams', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/66d08f49-ec17-52ff-a25d-28f2daf6ad74', 'word_count': 174, 'uri': 'nyt://article/66d08f49-ec17-52ff-a25d-28f2daf6ad74'}, {'abstract': 'Jon Meacham on how Clinton’s chronicle of loss in 2016 compares with those of defeated candidates past.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/09/12/books/review/jon-meacham-hillary-clinton-what-happened-presidential-election.html', 'snippet': 'Jon Meacham on how Clinton’s chronicle of loss in 2016 compares with those of defeated candidates past.', 'lead_paragraph': 'She had packed for victory. There had been a white suit for election night at the Javits Center beneath a glass ceiling; white was the color of the suffragists who, a century earlier, had at last won the franchise for women. But now, in the morning hours after Donald J. Trump’s White House upset, Hillary Clinton donned gray and purple for her concession to the country. The sartorial detail, which Clinton shares in her new memoir of the 2016 campaign, is a touch worthy of Plutarch, who observed that “a small thing … often makes a greater revelation of a character than battles where thousands die.” For there had been a different plan. The gray and purple, she writes, was the “one I had intended to wear on my first trip to Washington as President Elect.”', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/01/books/01LongViewMeacham1/01LongViewMeacham1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/10/01/books/01LongViewMeacham1/01LongViewMeacham1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/01/books/01LongViewMeacham1/01LongViewMeacham1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/01/books/01LongViewMeacham1/01LongViewMeacham1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/10/01/books/01LongViewMeacham1/01LongViewMeacham1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/01/books/01LongViewMeacham1/01LongViewMeacham1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/01/books/01LongViewMeacham1/01LongViewMeacham1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘What Happened’? They Lost. With Her Memoir, Hillary Clinton Joins a Haunted Club', 'kicker': 'The Long View', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Sad, Unsung Literature of Presidential Defeat', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'What Happened (Book)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clinton, Hillary Rodham', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2016', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-09-12T17:30:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jon Meacham', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Meacham', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f626540c-5697-59fc-bdc0-ce3aeb5499b6', 'word_count': 4017, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f626540c-5697-59fc-bdc0-ce3aeb5499b6'}, {'abstract': 'The State of New Jersey took over running the district because of low performance, but real educational progress has been slow in coming.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/09/12/nyregion/20-years-newark-schools-regain-control-baraka.html', 'snippet': 'The State of New Jersey took over running th