 'nyt://article/98dbb66b-7d85-5dfd-9505-2367f5405542', 'word_count': 788, 'uri': 'nyt://article/98dbb66b-7d85-5dfd-9505-2367f5405542'}, {'abstract': 'Though we may still pop headphones in to watch a YouTube rant, social media has cultivated its own mute visual culture.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/09/13/movies/silent-film-youtube-videos.html', 'snippet': 'Though we may still pop headphones in to watch a YouTube rant, social media has cultivated its own mute visual culture.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The summer’s hottest destination for video entertainment is a U.K.-based social media brand called LADbible. In July alone, the viral clips that churn out of its Facebook page were viewed more than 3 billion times. Though the site is nominally branded around young British men, its offerings hold an oddly universal appeal. On a recent afternoon, it served up videos of a guy accidentally hitting himself in the head with a baseball bat; a pizza being made out of French fries; a dog bathing in a Jacuzzi; a woodworker crafting a salad bowl; a tourist riding a slide down the Great Wall of China and a manatee kissing a snorkeler.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/14/arts/14SILENT3/14SILENT3-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/09/14/arts/14SILENT3/14SILENT3-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/14/arts/14SILENT3/14SILENT3-thumbLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/14/arts/14SILENT3/14SILENT3-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 444, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/09/14/arts/14SILENT3/14SILENT3-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 444}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/14/arts/14SILENT3/14SILENT3-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 561, 'width': 758, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/14/arts/14SILENT3/14SILENT3-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 561, 'width': 758, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Silent Film Returns — on Social Media', 'kicker': "Critic's Notebook", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Silent Film Returns', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Media', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Facebook Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Video Recordings, Downloads and Streaming', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'BBDO Worldwide', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'YouTube.com', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-09-13T14:13:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Amanda Hess', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Amanda', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hess', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bf0b2ee7-c45f-5b27-9eed-67ca0dd8d4b4', 'word_count': 1480, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bf0b2ee7-c45f-5b27-9eed-67ca0dd8d4b4'}, {'abstract': 'Increasingly frequent wildfires fed by a warming climate could turn the park’s dense forests into sparser woodlands.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/09/13/climate/yellowstone-western-fires-in-two-forests.html', 'snippet': 'Increasingly frequent wildfires fed by a warming climate could turn the park’s dense forests into sparser woodlands.', 'lead_paragraph': 'YELLOWSTONE NATIONAL PARK, Wyo. — This is a tale of two forests, Densetown and Stumptown, whose paths diverged after a succession of wildfires. One illustrates the historic resilience of the dense Yellowstone pinelands; the other portends a much sparser future for these forests under climate change.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/08/25/climate/yellowstone-illo/yellowstone-illo-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/08/25/climate/yellowstone-illo/yellowstone-illo-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/08/25/climate/yellowstone-illo/yellowstone-illo-thumbLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/08/25/climate/yellowstone-illo/yellowstone-illo-articleLarge-v4.jpg', 'height': 297, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/08/25/climate/yellowstone-illo/yellowstone-illo-articleLarge-v4.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 297}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/08/25/climate/yellowstone-illo/yellowstone-illo-jumbo-v4.jpg', 'height': 507, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo',