954865aabe16'}, {'abstract': 'What can be done for the next girl who wakes up with her clothes inside out and her world ripped apart?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/09/13/opinion/campus-rape-devos-title-ix.html', 'snippet': 'What can be done for the next girl who wakes up with her clothes inside out and her world ripped apart?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last week I wrote a column praising Betsy DeVos for announcing that the Department of Education would revisit the Obama administration’s 2011 “guidance” on campus sexual assault. The new guidelines, often interpreted with Procrustean severity by nervous campus administrators, had all but eliminated elementary aspects of due process for the accused.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/14/opinion/13stephensWeb/15stephensWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/09/14/opinion/13stephensWeb/15stephensWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/14/opinion/13stephensWeb/15stephensWeb-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/14/opinion/13stephensWeb/15stephensWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 433, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/09/14/opinion/13stephensWeb/15stephensWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 433}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/14/opinion/13stephensWeb/15stephensWeb-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 738, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/14/opinion/13stephensWeb/15stephensWeb-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1477, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Campus Rape, a Survivor’s Story', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Columnist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Crimes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Education Department (US)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'DeVos, Elizabeth (1958- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Turner, Brock Allen', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-09-13T15:34:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bret Stephens', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bret', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stephens', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/d1ee2256-b276-578b-8a11-2f43d0f02664', 'word_count': 1311, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d1ee2256-b276-578b-8a11-2f43d0f02664'}, {'abstract': 'Cliffs soar skyward; torrents stream down. This is a nature as a theater of big, dwarfing effects.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/09/13/arts/design/chinese-landscapes-at-the-met-if-those-mountains-could-talk.html', 'snippet': 'Cliffs soar skyward; torrents stream down. This is a nature as a theater of big, dwarfing effects.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If you’ve seen only ash-aired Beijing, or that architectural Oz, Shanghai, you haven’t seen China. Most of the country is wide-open space, green and blue: hills, plains, water. And it was an escape to that openness that some Chinese urbanites — clerks pinned to desks, scholar-officials swimming in a shark-tank imperial court — yearned for in centuries past. Their dream was to sit in on a terrace halfway up a mountain, with tea steeping, an ink-brush at hand, a friend at the door and a waterfall splashing nearby. Not just for vacation. Forever.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/15/arts/15landscape2/15landscape2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 310, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/09/15/arts/15landscape2/15landscape2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 310}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/15/arts/15landscape2/15landscape2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 530, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/15/arts/15landscape2/15landscape2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1059, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/15/arts/15landscape2/15landscape2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/09/15/arts/15landscape2/15landscape2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/15/arts/15landscape2/15landscape2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Chinese Landscapes at the Met: If Those Mountains Could Talk', 'kicker': 'Art Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'If Those Mountains Could Speak', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Metropolitan Museum of Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Streams and Mountains Without End: Landscape Traditions of China (Exhibit)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-09-13T15:37:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Holland Cotter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Holland', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cotter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/5cec3f48-b1c0-56f6-8f1c-2ad72619c0e4', 'word_count': 1299, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5cec3f48-b1c0-56f6-8f1c-2ad72619c0e4'}, {'abstract': 'President Trump has been wooing Democrats and pressing Republicans for fast action on a rewrite of the tax code, but huge hurdles remain.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/09/13/us/politics/republican-tax-overhaul-timeline-september.html', 'snippet': 'President Trump has been wooing Democrats and pressing Republicans for fast action on a rewrite of the tax code, but huge hurdles remain.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — President Trump is doubling down this week on his bid to remake the tax code, meeting with Democrats, tying tax legislation to hurricane recovery and dispatching his economic team to Capitol Hill almost daily to prod lawmakers into action.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/14/us/14dc-taxes