one, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/abb03e89-dadc-5842-a0fb-67a35519370b', 'word_count': 887, 'uri': 'nyt://article/abb03e89-dadc-5842-a0fb-67a35519370b'}, {'abstract': 'As policy makers, teachers, and parents work to expand pre-K programs, here are three books on what children really need.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/09/13/books/understanding-early-education.html', 'snippet': 'As policy makers, teachers, and parents work to expand pre-K programs, here are three books on what children really need.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Across the country, school reformers are pushing for the expansion of publicly funded early education. In New York, Mayor Bill de Blasio, who won the Democratic mayoral primary on Sept. 12, ran on a platform in 2013 centered on the expansion of prekindergarten education to all 4-year-olds; now, in a proposal he is calling “3-K for All,” he plans to reach 3-year-olds, as well. The science is clear: Quality early education has long-term benefits. Still, not everyone is on the same page about what young learners really need. Below, one writer examines the landscape of prekindergarten education across the country, another instructs adults on how to understand young children, and a third will be a resource for parents in the process of selecting a school for their child.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/12/books/12newsbookprek6/12newsbookprek6-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/09/12/books/12newsbookprek6/12newsbookprek6-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/12/books/12newsbookprek6/12newsbookprek6-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/12/books/12newsbookprek6/12newsbookprek6-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 303, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/09/12/books/12newsbookprek6/12newsbookprek6-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 303}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/12/books/12newsbookprek6/12newsbookprek6-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 517, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/12/books/12newsbookprek6/12newsbookprek6-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1034, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '3 Books on the Importance of Early Education', 'kicker': 'Newsbook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Importance of Being Little: What Young Children Really Need From Grownups (Book)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Most Important Year: Pre-Kindergarten and the Future of Our Children (Book)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Christakis, Erika', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bouffard, Suzanne', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tyre, Peg', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Good School: How Smart Parents Get Their Kids the Education They Deserve (Book)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}]