pg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 732, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/13/t-magazine/tmag-rafael-slide-XSEK/tmag-rafael-slide-XSEK-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1753, 'width': 1252, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/13/t-magazine/tmag-rafael-slide-XSEK/tmag-rafael-slide-XSEK-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/09/13/t-magazine/tmag-rafael-slide-XSEK/tmag-rafael-slide-XSEK-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/13/t-magazine/tmag-rafael-slide-XSEK/tmag-rafael-slide-XSEK-thumbLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Profile in Style: Rafael de Cárdenas', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ARCHITECTURE', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'de Cardenas, Rafael', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-09-13T17:22:02+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'T Magazine', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/508b2272-da7b-5a84-a88b-dd922b339d7d', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/508b2272-da7b-5a84-a88b-dd922b339d7d'}, {'abstract': 'The architect shares his many obsessions and inspirations.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/09/13/t-magazine/design/rafael-de-cardenas.html', 'snippet': 'The architect shares his many obsessions and inspirations.', 'lead_paragraph': 'While working as a designer for Calvin Klein in the 1990s, Rafael de Cárdenas read an article in The New York Times that changed his life. It was a profile on the then-new Guggenheim Museum in Spain, entitled ‘‘The Miracle in Bilbao.’’ Critic Herbert Muschamp described the building as ‘‘the reincarnation of Marilyn Monroe.’’ The seductive structure, and Muschamp’s words, impressed de Cárdenas, who had recently graduated from the Rhode Island School of Design’s fashion program. ‘‘I remember thinking, Wow, that’s the best description of a building I’ve ever heard,’’ he says. A few years later, he enrolled at U.C.L.A.’s architecture school, where he studied under the revolutionary architect Greg Lynn, for whom he would work after graduation.', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '102', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/13/t-magazine/tmag-rafael-slide-M5QF/tmag-rafael-slide-M5QF-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/09/13/t-magazine/tmag-rafael-slide-M5QF/tmag-rafael-slide-M5QF-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/13/t-magazine/tmag-rafael-slide-M5QF/tmag-rafael-slide-M5QF-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/13/t-magazine/tmag-rafael-slide-M5QF/tmag-rafael-slide-M5QF-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 424, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/09/13/t-magazine/tmag-rafael-slide-M5QF/tmag-rafael-slide-M5QF-articleLarge.