line': {'original': 'By Gail Collins', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gail', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Collins', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/6222f183-176e-5f8a-ae35-b0a346efd07a', 'word_count': 828, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6222f183-176e-5f8a-ae35-b0a346efd07a'}, {'abstract': 'The Federal Reserve doesn’t do enough to restrain out-of-control prices for stocks, houses and other assets. It should, and Donald Trump can help.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/09/14/opinion/trump-federal-reserve-markets.html', 'snippet': 'The Federal Reserve doesn’t do enough to restrain out-of-control prices for stocks, houses and other assets. It should, and Donald Trump can help.', 'lead_paragraph': ' The Federal Reserve arguably has more influence on the daily lives of Americans than any other government agency. In the coming year President Trump has a chance to appoint or replace five of the central bank’s seven governors, including the vice chairman, Stanley Fischer, and possibly the chairwoman, Janet Yellen.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/14/opinion/14sharma/14sharma-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/09/14/opinion/14sharma/14sharma-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/14/opinion/14sharma/14sharma-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/14/opinion/14sharma/14sharm