'_id': 'nyt://article/df1d187c-5266-5e29-b478-37a99c4720ee', 'word_count': 848, 'uri': 'nyt://article/df1d187c-5266-5e29-b478-37a99c4720ee'}, {'abstract': 'The relatively unknown story of photography’s important role in the Chicano movement is featured in a new exhibition at the Autry Museum of the American West.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2017/09/14/making-chicano-life-visible/', 'snippet': 'The relatively unknown story of photography’s important role in the Chicano movement is featured in a new exhibition at the Autry Museum of the American West.', 'lead_paragraph': 'From 1967 to 1977, La Raza, the Los Angeles newspaper turned magazine, provided a vital and dynamic forum for Chicano political and cultural expression. Employing a range of disciplines, including photojournalism, graphic art, satire, poetry and political commentary, it was both chronicler and participant in the Mexican-American struggle for equality and justice. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Making Chicano Life Visible', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Archives and Records', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mexican-Americans', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Race and Ethnicity', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Getty Foundation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Farm Workers of America', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-09-14T08:00:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By Maurice Berger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Maurice', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Berger', 'qualifier': None, 'ti