eive', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'How to Quit a Major Magazine Job', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Leive, Cindi', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Glamour (Magazine)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Magazines', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Conde Nast Publications Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-09-14T14:36:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Katherine Rosman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Katherine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/826ae9fe-03bb-5a5e-b544-b5d86def2f51', 'word_count': 1480, 'uri': 'nyt://article/826ae9fe-03bb-5a5e-b544-b5d86def2f51'}, {'abstract': 'The N.F.L. has a jam-packed slate, including a rematch of last year’s N.F.C. championship game. Here’s who we think will win.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/09/14/sports/nfl-week-2-predictions-schedule.html', 'snippet': 'The N.F.L. has a jam-packed slate, including a rematch of last year’s N.F.C. championship game. Here’s who we think will win.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Every team that won last week is Super Bowl-bound, and every team that lost is convinced it was a fluke. That is the beauty of Week 2; the predictive nature of Week 1 is entirely dependent on how your team fared. Unlike last week, when Hurricane Irma forced a postponement of a game between Miami and Tampa Bay, all 32 teams will play. Here’s how we think things will play out.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'cr