e quite like the home in “Mother!”, the new film from Darren Aronofsky. Jennifer Lawrence plays the title character who lives in (and doesn’t ever leave) an isolated house with her husband (Javier Bardem). Their peaceful life is disrupted when visitors (Michelle Pfeiffer and Ed Harris) arrive. And in this scene, even more visitors show up to ruin paradise. At the Toronto International Film Festival, where the film played ahead of its theatrical release Friday, Mr. Aronofsky spoke about his interest in biblical narratives, his decision to shoot on film and the house he used for the movie. Here are excerpts from the conversation.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Darren Aronofsky Narrates a Scene From ‘Mother!’', 'kicker': 'Anatomy of a Scene', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ARONOFSKY, DARREN', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lawrence, Jennifer', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Mother! (Movie)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-09-14T15:19:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mekado Murphy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mekado', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Murphy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/265618e5-f094-5f5a-9f43-c89d8275944b', 'word_count': 464, 'uri': 'nyt://article/265618e5-f094-5f5a-9f43-c89d8275944b'}, {'abstract': 'The kingdom has arrested 16 people — including clerics, scholars and a prince — and it is not clear if they have been charged.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/09/14/world/middleeast/saudi-arabia-clerics.html', 'snippet': 'The kingdom has arrested 16 people — inclu