d': 'nyt://article/b5e1e5c1-ceb2-5f00-ba96-4286d5c576ca', 'word_count': 1591, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b5e1e5c1-ceb2-5f00-ba96-4286d5c576ca'}, {'abstract': 'Welcoming the stranger is one of the great moral traditions liberals have.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/09/15/opinion/conservative-professors.html', 'snippet': 'Welcoming the stranger is one of the great moral traditions liberals have.', 'lead_paragraph': 'These days, the news is full of sensational stories of violent campus mobs shutting down conservative speakers and freaked-out college administrators treating rioters with kid gloves. Such stories offer excellent fodder for critics who are eager to condemn university culture. But I believe they distract from a deeper, subtler intellectual problem on the modern campus: the profound alienation of professors who don’t hold the mainstream political views and are treated as outsiders as a result.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/15/opinion/15arthurbrooks/15arthurbrooks-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/09/15/opinion/15arthurbrooks/15arthurbrooks-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/15/opinion/15arthurbrooks/15arthurbrooks-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/15/opinion/15arthurbrooks/15arthurbrooks-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 479, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/09/15/opinion/15arthurbrooks/15arthurbrooks-a