n the morgue is one of Hurricane Harvey’s mysteries.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HOUSTON — It was a hard choice, but in the end it was no choice at all. A small rescue boat had come up the driveway, offering help. Carl Ellis was with his frail, 73-year-old mother, Wilma Jean. The boat had room for one.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/17/us/17rescue-02-SUB/17rescue-02-SUB-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/09/17/us/17rescue-02-SUB/17rescue-02-SUB-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/17/us/17rescue-02-SUB/17rescue-02-SUB-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/17/us/17rescue-02-SUB/17rescue-02-SUB-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 339, 'width': 507, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/17/us/17rescue-02-SUB/17rescue-02-SUB-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 339, 'width': 507, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Saved From Harvey’s Floodwaters, Twice. So How Did She End Up Dead?', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Twice Saved From Houston Floods but Still, Mysteriously, a Victim', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hurricane Harvey (2017)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drownings', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Houston (Tex)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-09-16T17:05:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Shaila Dewan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Shaila', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dewan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/05785286-3044-560a-abbf-38238e152d79', 'word_count': 1916, 'uri': 'nyt://article/05785286-3044-560a-abbf-38238e152d79'}, {'abstract': 'All eyes will be on the new American president at his first United Nations General Assembly as international leaders take his measure.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/09/16/world/americas/the-big-question-as-the-un-gathers-what-to-make-of-trump.html', 'snippet': 'All eyes will be on the new American president at his first United Nations General Assembly as international leaders take his measure.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Every year, the president heads to New York to welcome world leaders to the United Nations General Assembly. He gives a speech and meets with an endless string of foreign potentates to discuss a dizzying array of complicated, often intractable issues.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Big Question as the U.N. Gathers: What to Make of Trump?', 'kicker': 'News Analysis', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'World’s Eyes On President As U.N. Meets', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'General Assembly (UN)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-09-16T17:07:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Washington', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter Baker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Baker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News Analysis', '_id': 'nyt://article/6f33b652-2982-5ebb-8a3f-bd5d56641531', 'word_count': 1267, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6f33b652-2982-5ebb-8a3f-bd5d56641531'}, {'abstract': 'President Trump has reason to worry about China, but he should seek areas of agreement with Beijing and enlist it in addressing global problems.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/09/16/opinion/sunday/the-china-puzzle.html', 'snippet': 'President Trump has reason to worry about China, but he should seek areas of agreement with Beijing and enlist it in addressing global problems.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Steve Bannon, the former presidential confidante, was as apocalyptic as ever about China on the eve of his trip to Hong Kong. The man who had all but declared “economic war” with China in earlier interviews said to a Times reporter, “A hundred years from now, this is what they’ll remember — what we did to confront China on its rise to world domination.” On arrival, in a speech to a big investor conference, he seemed to have softened a bit, praising China’s leadership and offering hopes that a trade war could be averted.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/17/opinion/sunday/17sun1/17sun1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/09/17/opinion/sunday/17sun1/17sun1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/17/opinion/sunday/17sun1/17sun1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/17/opinion/sunday/17sun1/17sun1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 359, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/09/17/opinion/sunday/17sun1/17sun1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 359}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/17/opinion/sunday/17sun1/17sun1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 612, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/17/opinion/sunday/17sun1/17sun1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1225, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The China Puzzle', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The China Puzzle', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Xi Jinping', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bannon, Stephen K', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-09-16T17:41:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/77b98b9a-e66b-5b14-b4a5-3459054d418e', 'word_count': 1113, 'uri': 'nyt://article/77b98b9a-e66b-5b14-b4a5-3459054d418e'}, {'abstract': 'A secret transcript of a recent conversation between the Almighty and a televangelist.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/09/16/opinion/sunday/jim-bakker-evangelicals.html', 'snippet': 'A secret transcript of a recent conversation between the Almighty and a televangelist.', 'lead_paragraph': ' The famous televangelist Jim Bakker, who is preaching again on television after a rape accusation and a prison term for financial fraud, recently warned that Christians would start an armed insurrection if President Trump were impeached. “If it happens, there will be civil war in the United States of America,” Bakker told his television audience. “The Christians will finally come out of the shadows, because we are going to be shut up permanently if we’re not careful.”', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/17/opinion/sunday/17kristof/17kristof-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/09/17/opinion/sunday/17kristof/17kristof-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/17/opinion/sunday/17kristof/17kristof-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/17/opinion/sunday/17kristof/17kristof-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 384, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/09/17/opinion/sunday/17kristof/17kristof-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 384}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/17/opinion/sunday/17kristof/17kristof-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 655, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/17/opinion/sunday/17kristof/17kristof-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1311, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘Enough Already,’ Said God', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Columnist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '‘Enough Already,’ Said God', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bakker, Jim', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Evangelical Movement', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-09-16T18:20:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicholas Kristof', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kristof', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/20a0a141-a218-5e53-87dc-80cb387c7677', 'word_count': 874, 'uri': 'nyt://article/20a0a141-a218-5e53-87dc-80cb387c7677'}, {'abstract': 'The stalemate strategy didn’t work there. It won’t in Afghanistan either.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/09/16/opinion/trump-afghanistan-vietnam-war.html', 'snippet': 'The stalemate strategy didn’t work there. It won’t in Afghanistan either.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In August 1965, a resolute President Lyndon Johnson said: “America wins the wars that she undertakes. Make no mistake about it.” But the strategy on which he committed America to its ill-fated intervention in Vietnam that year did not aim at winning, but at not losing. McGeorge Bundy, Johnson’s national security adviser, later admitted as much to a biographer, saying that he had personally approved a strategy that used just enough military pressure to achieve a battlefield stalemate, which “would eventually compel the Vietnamese Communists to compromise their objectives,” forcing them to the negotiating table or to a Korea-style armistice.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/17/opinion/sunday/17elliott-vietnamSUB/17elliott-vietnamSUB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/09/17/opinion/sunday/17elliott-vietnamSUB/17elliott-vietnamSUB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/17/opinion/sunday/17elliott-vietnamSUB/17elliott-vietnamSUB-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/17/opinion/sunday/17elliott-vietnamSUB/17elliott-vietnamSUB-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 402, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/09/17/opinion/sunday/17elliott-vietnamSUB/17elliott-vietnamSUB-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 402}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/17/opinion/sunday/17elliott-vietnamSUB/17elliott-vietnamSUB-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 686, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/17/opinion/sunday/17elliott-vietnamSUB/17elliott-vietnamSUB-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1372, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'What Trump Needs to Learn From Vietnam', 'kicker': "Vietnam '67", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What Trump Needs to Learn From Vietnam', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vietnam War', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Johnson, Lyndon Baines', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGHANISTAN', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Vietnam', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-09-16T18:27:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Elliott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Elliott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/ca9a86ab-5816-56a1-8394-235ca3fb7b05', 'word_count': 1007, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ca9a86ab-5816-56a1-8394-235ca3fb7b05'}, {'abstract': 'Giancarlo Stanton will set a record if he hits 62 homers. Or will he?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/09/16/opinion/sunday/giancarlo-stanton-baseball-homeruns.html', 'snippet': 'Giancarlo Stanton will set a record if he hits 62 homers. Or will he?', 'lead_paragraph': 'For Major League Baseball, 2017 has been a season of extremes. The Los Angeles Dodgers went on an extraordinary tear, winning 84 percent of the time during one 67-game stretch. Then they pulled a U-ie and lost all but one of their next 17 games. The Cleveland Indians entered the weekend Friday night having triumphed in 22 straight games, an American League record.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/17/opinion/17sun2web/17sun2web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/09/17/opinion/17sun2web/17sun2web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/17/opinion/17sun2web/17sun2web-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/17/opinion/17sun2web/17sun2web-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 374, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/09/17/opinion/17sun2web/17sun2web-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 374}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/17/opinion/17sun2web/17sun2web-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 638, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/17/opinion/17sun2web/17sun2web-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1275, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Baseball Theory of Relativity', 'kicker': 'Editorial Notebook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Baseball Theory of Relativity', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stanton, Giancarlo', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Major League Baseball', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Miami Marlins', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'AARON, HANK', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ruth, Babe', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-09-16T18:29:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Clyde Haberman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Clyde', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Haberman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/a774714a-2d4f-5e48-a2a7-b5210ce7f587', 'word_count': 484, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a774714a-2d4f-5e48-a2a7-b5210ce7f587'}, {'abstract': 'The veteran pols on either side of the vituperative, vertiginous Brexit debate spar.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/09/16/opinion/sunday/brexit-blair-farage-dowd.html', 'snippet': 'The veteran pols on either side of the vituperative, vertiginous Brexit debate spar.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — It seems like an impossible feat. But Tony Blair has done it. He has made himself even less popular in Britain.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/17/opinion/sunday/17dowd/17dowd-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/09/17/opinion/sunday/17dowd/17dowd-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/17/opinion/sunday/17dowd/17dowd-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/17/opinion/sunday/17dowd/17dowd-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 606, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/09/17/opinion/sunday/17dowd/17dowd-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 606}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/17/opinion/sunday/17dowd/17dowd-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1014, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/17/opinion/sunday/17dowd/17dowd-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 2028, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Boys of Brexit: Tony Blair and Nigel Farage', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Columnist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Boys of Brexit', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Blair, Tony', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Farage, Nigel (1964- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Great Britain Withdrawal from EU (Brexit)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-09-16T18:30:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Maureen Dowd', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Maureen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dowd', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/6f912a4e-acd2-5f34-b527-0fdd7388daa1', 'word_count': 2650, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6f912a4e-acd2-5f34-b527-0fdd7388daa1'}, {'abstract': 'A man called me a liar, and it reminded me of all the people who have doubted me.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/09/16/opinion/sunday/amber-tamblyn-james-woods.html', 'snippet': 'A man called me a liar, and it reminded me of all the people who have doubted me.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When I was 21, I went into the office of a producer of the television show I was starring in to discuss a big problem. By this point I had been acting for more than a decade, and the show was very successful and beloved. Still, I was nervous about facing the firing squad of Emmys that sat behind him and saying what I had to say.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/06/24/opinion/sunday/24Tamblyn-1505574296961/17Tamblyn-1505574296961-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 397, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/06/24/opinion/sunday/24Tamblyn-1505574296961/17Tamblyn-1505574296961-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 397}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/06/24/opinion/sunday/24Tamblyn-1505574296961/17Tamblyn-1505574296961-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 677, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/06/24/opinion/sunday/24Tamblyn-1505574296961/17Tamblyn-1505574296961-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1354, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/06/24/opinion/sunday/24Tamblyn-150557