ttle of the Civil War.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/09/18/insider/1851-new-york-times-born-into-racial-turmoil-that-has-never-ended.html', 'snippet': 'In issue No. 1, The Times described the recent killing of a slaveholder in an attack that has been called the first battle of the Civil War.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Happy birthday? Not entirely.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/08/insider/08insider-birthday/08insider-birthday-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/10/08/insider/08insider-birthday/08insider-birthday-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/08/insider/08insider-birthday/08insider-birthday-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/08/insider/08insider-birthday/08insider-birthday-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 722, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/10/08/insider/08insider-birthday/08insider-birthday-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 722}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/08/insider/08insider-birthday/08insider-birthday-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 851, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/08/insider/08insider-birthday/08insider-birthday-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1619, 'width': 1345, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '1851 | Born Into a Racial Turmoil That Has Never Ended', 'kicker': 'Looking Back', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Slavery (Historical)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Raymond, Henry Jarvis', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil War (US) (1861-65)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Times', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fugitives', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-09-18T17:24:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Insider', 'section_name': 'Times Insider', 'byline': {'original': 'By David W. Dunlap', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Dunlap', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fa25f6a4-8041-5238-970d-448e26e1a3b4', 'word_count': 790, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fa25f6a4-8041-5238-970d-448e26e1a3b4'}, {'abstract': 'The producers of the closed Broadway musical will open Samovarchik, the foods of the samurai and more news.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/09/18/dining/pierogi-samovarchik-easy-fermenter.html', 'snippet': 'The producers of the closed Broadway musical will open Samovarchik, the foods of the samurai and more news.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After the musical “Natasha, Pierre & the Great Comet of 1812” closed on Broadway this month, the producers — including Darren Sussman and Roman Gambourg — realized there was such enthusiasm for the production that they decided to keep up the interest by opening a place to serve pirogi. (Theatergoers were given a small box containing one potato pirogen at the start of the show.) Samovarchik, a little spot with a counter and a few seats indoors and out, offers a menu of Russian specialties made from the recipes of Lena Gambourg, a native of St. Petersburg, a real-estate broker and Mr. Gambourg’s mother. Pirogi, pelmeni dumplings, savory kachapuri pastries, borscht and beef stroganoff are among the richly alluring temptations: Samovarchik, 11 Stanton Street (Bowery), 646-882-0333.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/20/dining/20Burner1/20Burner1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/09/20/dining/20Burner1/20Burner1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/20/dining/20Burner1/20Burner1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/20/dining/20Burner1/20Burner1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/09/20/dining/20Burner1/20Burner1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/20/dining/20Burner1/20Burner1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/20/dining/20Burner1/20Burner1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Pirogi From ‘the Great Comet of 1812’ Hit the Lower East Side', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None