en-downie-uxua-casa-hotel.html', 'snippet': 'A new Malick Sidibé retrospective, designer building blocks — and a dream house in Brazil.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Next month, Malick Sidibé, the photographer known for his black-and-white images of youth culture in Mali, will have his biggest retrospective since his death last year. Opening at the Fondation Cartier in Paris, ‘‘Malick Sidibé: Mali Twist’’ features more than 125 never-before-seen images, to be displayed alongside his iconic shots of sub-Saharan hipsters showing off their bell-bottoms, wristwatches, radios and James Brown records, and couples dancing barefoot, their heads nearly touching, to music we can no longer hear.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/15/t-magazine/tmag-thisthat-slide-A5NP/tmag-thisthat-slide-A5NP-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/09/15/t-magazine/tmag-thisthat-slide-A5NP/tmag-thisthat-slide-A5NP-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/15/t-magazine/tmag-thisthat-slide-A5NP/tmag-thisthat-slide-A5NP-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/15/t-magazine/tmag-thisthat-slide-A5NP/tmag-thisthat-slide-A5NP-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 411, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/09/15/t-magazine/tmag-thisthat-slide-A5NP/tmag-thisthat-slide-A5NP-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 411}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'imag