nfiction best-seller list.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/19/business/19oreillybook-1/19oreillybook-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/09/19/business/19oreillybook-1/19oreillybook-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/19/business/19oreillybook-1/19oreillybook-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/19/business/19oreillybook-1/19oreillybook-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/09/19/business/19oreillybook-1/19oreillybook-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/19/business/19oreillybook-1/19oreillybook-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/19/business/19oreillybook-1/19oreillybook-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Will Bill O’Reilly’s Latest ‘Killing’ Book Climb the Charts?', 'kicker': 'Book News', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Preorders Sag for Latest Book in O’Reilly’s Best-Selling ‘Killing’ Series', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': "O'Reilly, Bill", 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Killing England: The Brutal Struggle for American Independence (Book)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-09-18T20:48:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alexandra Alter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alexandra', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/51864000-178c-5b90-9d89-69dc0665e137', 'word_count': 953, 'uri': 'nyt://article/51864000-178c-5b90-9d89-69dc0665e137'}, {'abstract': 'Inspired by a look on Gabriela Hearst’s spring runway, we tracked down updated versions of the classic staple you can buy now.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/09/18/t-magazine/lightweight-jacket-khaki.html', 'snippet': 'Inspired by a look on Gabriela Hearst’s spring runway, we tracked down updated versions of the classic staple you can buy now.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A khaki jacket in a light cotton or linen has long been a staple in the closets of men and women — traditionally worn on exotic journeys to tropical locales. Yves Saint Laurent’s famous ’60s safari shirts (which he also wore himself) are an enduring example of the appeal and versatility of the style. They were inspired by his muse, the French model Danielle Luquet de Saint Germain, who was fond of wearing men’s clothing and whom Saint Laurent also credited as the genesis of his Le Smoking design. At Gabriela Hearst’s spring/summer 2018 show in New York, she sent out a limited-edition putty-colored wrap blazer and matching skirt, in sustainable linen, that interpreted the classic travel suit in a wonderfully sexy, modern way. While you wait for her designs to hit stores, here are a few versions of the timeless design you can buy now — perfect for any imminent adventures.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/18/t-magazine/18tmag-shoppable1/18tmag-shoppable1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 899, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/09/18/t-magazine/18tmag-shoppable1/18tmag-shoppable1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 899}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/18/t-magazine/18tmag-shoppable1/18tmag-shoppable1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 684, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/18/t-magazine/18tmag-shoppable1/18tmag-shoppable1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1367, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/18/t-magazine/18tmag-shoppable1/18tmag-shoppable1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/09/18/t-magazine/18tmag-shoppable1/18tmag-shoppable1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/18/t-magazine/18tmag-shoppable1/18tmag-shoppable1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Six Lightweight Jackets That Are Perfect for Travel', 'kicker': 'Instant Gratification', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Yves Saint Laurent', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hearst, Gabriela', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-09-18T20:51:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alexa Brazilian', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alexa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brazilian', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/eafff18d-61d9-5818-97a6-3f66ecc7a237', 'word_count': 152, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eafff18d-61d9-5818-97a6-3f66ecc7a237'}, {'abstract': 'As world leaders gather at the United Nations for the world body’s annual General Assembly, a group of American state governors is taking an increasingly high-profile role on climate change.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/09/18/climate/climate-change-unga-governors.html', 'snippet': 'As world leaders gather at the United Nations for the world body’s annual General Assembly, a group of American state governors is taking an increasingly high-profile role on climate change.', 'lead_paragraph': 'UNITED NATIONS — Jerry Brown, the governor of California, huddled on Sunday night with European, Brazilian and small-island leaders — gathered here for the 72nd session of the United Nations General Assembly, which formally begins on Tuesday — and pledged to work with them on climate change. On Monday he met with António Guterres, the United Nations secretary general, to discuss the future of the Paris agreement.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/19/science/19CLIMATESTATES1/19CLIMATESTATES1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/09/19/science/19CLIMATESTATES1/19CLIMATESTATES1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/19/science/19CLIMATESTATES1/19CLIMATESTATES1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/19/science/19CLIMATESTATES1/19CLIMATESTATES1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/09/19/science/19CLIMATESTATES1/19CLIMATESTATES1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/19/science/19CLIMATESTATES1/19CLIMATESTATES1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/19/science/19CLIMATESTATES1/19CLIMATESTATES1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S. Governors at U.N. Assembly: ‘You Have Allies’ on Climate Change', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'General Assembly (UN)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Governors (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'States (US)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brown, Edmund G Jr', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United Nations F