lth-care-medicare.html', 'snippet': 'It will share the same flaws of “Medicare for all”-style systems around the world.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last week, Senator Bernie Sanders introduced “Medicare for all” legislation, which would enroll all Americans into the nation’s Medicare program within four years. Senator Sanders, the Vermont independent, argues that his proposal would create a system that “works not just for millionaires and billionaires, but for all of us.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/19/opinion/19chenweinberg/19chenweinberg-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/09/19/opinion/19chenweinberg/19chenweinberg-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/19/opinion/19chenweinberg/19chenweinberg-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/19/opinion/19chenweinberg/19chenweinberg-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1453, 'width': 1453, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/19/opinion/19chenweinberg/19chenweinberg-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/09/19/opinion/19chenweinberg/19chenweinberg-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/19/opinion/19chenweinberg/19chenweinberg-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Sanders Single-Payer Plan Is No Miracle Cure', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributors', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '‘Medicare for All’ Is No Miracle Cure', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sanders, Bernard', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Canada', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-09-19T07:21:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lanhee J. Chen and Micah Weinberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lanhee', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Chen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Micah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Weinberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/4529a56a-0a1f-5256-968e-bceb3e748415', 'word_count': 860, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4529a56a-0a1f-5256-968e-bceb3e748415'}, {'abstract': 'H.I.V. infection rates are falling in Africa, a sign that the AIDS epidemic could be brought to an end.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/09/19/opinion/in-africa-a-glimpse-of-hope-for-beating-hiv.html', 'snippet': 'H.I.V. infection rates are falling in Africa, a sign that the AIDS epidemic could be brought to an end.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A couple of years ago, European researchers began studying more than a thousand couples, gay and straight, in which one member had been infected with H.I.V. and the other hadn’t. These couples weren’t using condoms. But the infected partner was taking antiretrovirals successfully; the virus was suppressed, undetectable in the blood. The researchers published their results in July 2016 in the Journal of the American Medical Association.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/19/opinion/19fixesWeb/19fixesWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/09/19/opinion/19fixesWeb/19fixesWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/19/opinion/19fixesWeb/19fixesWeb-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/19/opinion/19fixesWeb/19fixesWeb-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/19/opinion/19fixesWeb/19fixesWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/09/19/opinion/19fixesWeb/19fixesWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/19/opinion/19fixesWeb/19fixesWeb-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Africa, a Glimpse of Hope for Beating H.I.V.', 'kicker': 'Fixes', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Acquired Immune Deficiency Syndrome', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tests (Medical)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Epidemics', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Journal of the American Medical Assn', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "President's Emergency Plan for AIDS Relief", 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homosexuality and Bisexuality', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Global Fund to Fight AIDS, Tuberculosis and Malaria', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'UNAIDS', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Birx, Deborah L', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bush, George W', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Leahy, Patrick J', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mugabe, Robert', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFRICA', 'rank': 15, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Harare (Zimbabwe)', 'rank': 16, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Malawi', 'rank': 17, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Lesotho', 'rank': 18, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-09-19T07:21:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tina Rosenberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/f04ed5e3-36fe-547c-b588-a7f70d850571', 'word_count': 1657, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f04ed5e3-36fe-547c-b588-a7f70d850571'}, {'abstract': 'Midtown traffic for the United Nations General Assembly is a reminder of the need for a plan to cut traffic and fund mass transit by adding tolls.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/09/19/opinion/editorials/manhattan-congestion-pricing-traffic.html', 'snippet': 'Midtown traffic for the United Nations General Assembly is a reminder of the need for a plan to cut traffic and fund mass transit by adding tolls.', 'lead_paragraph': 'New York commuters ably survived the “summer of hell” that Gov. Andrew Cuomo had forecast because of repair work at the hobbled Pennsylvania Station. Now Manhattan is enduring a different form of hellishness: severe Midtown traffic as the United Nations General Assembly convenes and world leaders gather. It’s a familiar late-summer headache. But it’s likely to be worse than usual this time, with extra streets closed off as protection for President Trump, ensconced for several days in his Fifth Avenue aerie.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/19/opinion/19tue2web/19tue2web-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/09/19/opinion/19tue2web/19tue2web-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/19/opinion/19tue2web/19tue2web-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/19/opinion/19tue2web/19tue2web-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/19/opinion/19tue2web/19tue2web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'ima