, Abraham', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Finkel, Eli J', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-09-19T07:21:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Brooks', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brooks', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/04410937-035e-5d92-bac3-3175719fabb4', 'word_count': 864, 'uri': 'nyt://article/04410937-035e-5d92-bac3-3175719fabb4'}, {'abstract': 'A police shooting in the Missouri town uncovered systemic bigotry. One man’s case shows how hard that is to overcome.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/09/19/opinion/editorials/ferguson-racism-fred-watson.html', 'snippet': 'A police shooting in the Missouri town uncovered systemic bigotry. One man’s case shows how hard that is to overcome.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Justice Department investigators examined the city of Ferguson, Mo., after a white police officer shot and killed an African-American teenager named Michael Brown in 2014, they found no grounds to charge the officer with federal civil rights violations. But they did uncover endemic bigotry among city officials, as well as policing that routinely violated black residents’ constitutional rights, with brutality and excessive, often bogus, enforcement.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/19/opinion/19tue3/19tue3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/09/19/opinion/19tue3/19tue3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/19/opinion/19tue3/19tue3-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/19/opinion/19tue3/19tue3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 702, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/09/19/opinion/19tue3/19tue3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 702}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/19/opinion/19tue3/19tue3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 876, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/19/opinion/19tue3/19tue3-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1123, 'width': 960, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Lingering Damage of Ferguson’s Racism', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Lingering Damage of Ferguson’s Racism', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police Brutality, Misconduct and Shootings', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ferguson (Mo)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Watson, Fred', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brown, Michael (1996-2014)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Race and Ethnicity', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Justice Department', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-09-19T07:21:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Editorials', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/0d6d1208-02cd-50ec-ad24-a38cd0f15dd6', 'word_count': 510, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0d6d1208-02cd-50ec-ad24-a38cd0f15dd6'}, {'abstract': 'After spending much of this year trying to kill the Affordable Care Act, House and Senate leaders try again with a worse plan.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/09/19/opinion/editorials/republican-healthcare-graham-cassidy.html', 'snippet': 'After spending much of this year trying to kill the Affordable Care Act, House and Senate leaders try again with a worse plan.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Republican lawmakers have wasted much of the year trying to repeal the Affordable Care Act, a move that would deprive millions of people of health insurance. They’re back at it. Like a bad sequel to a terrible movie, a proposal whose main architects are Bill Cassidy of Louisiana and Lindsey Graham of South Carolina would in many ways be worse than bills that came before. It would punish states like California and New York  that have done the most to increase access to health care and set in motion cuts to Medicaid, the federal-state program that provides insurance to nearly 70 million people, many of whom are disabled and elderly.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/19/opinion/19tue1/19tue1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/09/19/opinion/19tue1/19tue1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/19/opinion/19tue1/19tue1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/19/opinion/19tue1/19tue1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/09/19/opinion/19tue1/19tue1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/19/opinion/19tue1/19tue1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/19/opinion/19tue1/19tue1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1198, 'width': 1198, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Republican Health Care Zombie Is Back', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Health Care Zombie Is Back', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cassidy, Bill (1957- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Graham, Lindsey', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-09-19T07:21:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Editorials', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/19456696-c9ba-5154-bdab-99001b7fa5c3', 'word_count': 602, 'uri': 'nyt://article/19456696-c9ba-5154-bdab-99001b7fa5c3'}, {'abstract': 'Her style of talking has shaped how I hear other people’s words.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/09/19/opinion/language-female-friendship-mothers.html', 'snippet': 'Her style of talking has shaped how I hear other people’s words.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I was looking forward to having my friend Tamara over for dinner last year, since she had hosted me and my husband many times. But it didn’t turn out as I’d expected. Tamara kept trying to help in various ways, like retrieving items from the kitchen or clearing items from the table. Each time, I told her to please sit down, that I didn’t want her to help. But then she’d be up again.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/19/opinion/19tannenWeb/19tannenWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/09/19/opinion/19tannenWeb/19tannenWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/19/opinion/19tannenWeb/19tannenWeb-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/19/opinion/19tannenWeb/19tannenWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/09/19/opinion/19tannenWeb/19tannenWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/19/opinion/19tannenWeb/19tannenWeb-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 534, 'width': 949, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subty