Prune, writes one column a month for The New York Times Magazine. I don’t have anything to do with that, but I have edited a few of her essays in the past. We had a fine time working together, and kept in touch for a while. About a decade ago we introduced our toddlers for a play date while she cooked breakfast. It ended after her son hit mine over the head with a toy truck.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hunger and Desire, Stripped of Window Dressing, at Prune', 'kicker': 'Restaurant Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'At Prune, Simplicity Meets Nuance', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Prune (Manhattan, NY, Restaurant)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hamilton, Gabrielle', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Merriman, Ashley', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'East Village (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-09-19T15:59:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pete Wells', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pete', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wells', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/7c0a18a5-5749-5b95-9dcf-eb806335b8de', 'word_count': 1170, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7c0a18a5-5749-5b95-9dcf-eb806335b8de'}, {'abstract': 'Examples of the ancient Japanese technique that involves charring a specific kind of Japanese cedar.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2017/09/19/t-magazine/shou-sugi-ban-in-photos.html', 'snippet': 'Examples of the ancient Japanese technique that involves charring a specific kind of Japanese cedar.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Examples o