 {'abstract': 'The director Mahamat-Saleh Haroun gives voice to the people affected by Mr. Habré’s dictatorial government.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/09/19/movies/hissein-habre-review.html', 'snippet': 'The director Mahamat-Saleh Haroun gives voice to the people affected by Mr. Habré’s dictatorial government.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Documentarians have long struggled with how to depict the aftermaths of atrocities. Claude Lanzmann’s “Shoah” spreads its interviews out over more than nine hours, implicitly acknowledging the limitations of making a Holocaust film even as it serves as a record of survivors’ memories. Joshua Oppenheimer’s “The Act of Killing” goes for the throat: The director shows the former members of Indonesian death squads re-enacting their crimes.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/20/arts/20HISSEIN1/HISSEIN1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/09/20/arts/20HISSEIN1/HISSEIN1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/20/arts/20HISSEIN1/HISSEIN1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/20/arts/20HISSEIN1/HISSEIN1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 337, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/09/20/arts/20HISSEIN1/HISSEIN1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 337}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/20/arts/20HISSEIN1/HISSEIN1-jumbo.