o $120,000.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At a moment when some glitzy magazines — including Vanity Fair, Rolling Stone and Elle — have announced big changes during nervous financial times for legacy media, the world of nonprofit magazines has gotten a boost.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Whiting Foundation Announces New Grants for Magazines', 'kicker': 'Books News', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Magazines', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Whiting, Mrs Giles, Foundation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-09-19T18:40:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Williams', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Williams', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/68964b9b-8e54-550c-b691-bb7b2a49c197', 'word_count': 235, 'uri': 'nyt://article/68964b9b-8e54-550c-b691-bb7b2a49c197'}, {'abstract': 'In Mexico City, where a school collapsed, ordinary citizens used their bare hands to try to free the students trapped in the rubble.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/09/19/world/americas/mexico-earthquake.html', 'snippet': 'In Mexico City, where a school collapsed, ordinary citizens used their bare hands to try to free the students trapped in the rubble.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MEXICO CITY — A powerful earthquake struck Mexico on Tuesday afternoon, toppling buildings, killing children in a school that collapsed, rattling the capital and sending people flooding into the streets for the second time in just two weeks.', 'print_s