'subject', 'value': 'Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-09-20T18:38:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Emma G. Fitzsimmons', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Emma', 'middlename': 'G.', 'lastname': 'Fitzsimmons', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/89da465d-f63a-54cd-aa7e-18963c76eff0', 'word_count': 1498, 'uri': 'nyt://article/89da465d-f63a-54cd-aa7e-18963c76eff0'}, {'abstract': '“I wish he understood completely,” Senator Bill Cassidy, one of the bill’s co-authors, said of Mr. Kimmel, who has been a frequent critic of G.O.P. health legislation.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/09/20/arts/television/republican-health-bill-jimmy-kimmel.html', 'snippet': '“I wish he understood completely,” Senator Bill Cassidy, one of the bill’s co-authors, said of Mr. Kimmel, who has been a frequent critic of G.O.P. health legislation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Hours after Jimmy Kimmel unleashed a monologue attacking the latest bill that would undo much of the Affordable Care Act, two of the bill’s authors spent Wednesday morning defending the legislation against the late-night host, who in recent months has become an unlikely — and increasingly impassioned — critic.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/20/arts/21kimmel1/20latenight1-articleLarge.png', 'height': 334, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/09/20/arts/21kimmel1/20latenight1-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 334}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/20/arts/21kimmel1/20late