y at Equifax, one of the three major credit reporting companies, the private financial and personal details of as many as 143 million Americans have been exposed to hackers. We still don’t know what the full ramifications will be; the people who took this information — which includes birth dates, Social Security numbers and addresses — could hold on to it for as long as they want and deploy it in years to come.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/21/opinion/21covert/21covert-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/09/21/opinion/21covert/21covert-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/21/opinion/21covert/21covert-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/21/opinion/21covert/21covert-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 527, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/09/21/opinion/21covert/21covert-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 527}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/21/opinion/21covert/21covert-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 900, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/21/opinion/21covert/21covert-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1757, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Get Rid of Equifax', 'kicker': 'Contributing Op-Ed Writer', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Get Rid of Equifax', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Credit Scores', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nationalization of Industry', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Equifax Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'TransUnion LLC', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Experian PLC', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Personal Finances', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Consumer Protection', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computer Security', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-09-21T07:21:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bryce Covert', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bryce', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Covert', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/c44bc48a-d4ef-5f6b-8936-a89a68caae15', 'word_count': 915, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c44bc48a-d4ef-5f6b-8936-a89a68caae15'}, {'abstract': 'Photoville, the temporary photo festival underneath the Brooklyn Bridge, is featuring “emergicubes,” 4×4 foot wooden cubes displaying the work of 11 up-and-coming photographers from around the world.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2017/09/21/global-voices-and-emerging-photographers-at-photoville/', 'snippet': 'Photoville, the temporary photo festival underneath the Brooklyn Bridge, is featuring “emergicubes,” 4×4 foot wooden cubes displaying the work of 11 up-and-coming photographers from around the world.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Photoville, the temporary community of duplexes made by four-ton steel shipping containers underneath the Brooklyn Bridge, is featuring the work of 11 up-and-coming photographers from Africa, Asia, Latin America and the United States, displayed on four-foot wooden cubes. The photographers were chosen from participants in this year’s New York Portfolio Review — a free event sponsored by The New York Times Lens blog and The City University of New York Graduate School of Journalism. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Global Voices and Emerging Photographers at Photoville', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Documentary Films and Programs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn Bridge (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-09-21T08:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/62f9357a-4e66-55b8-a23b-3d31e524caf9', 'word_count': 595, 'uri': 'nyt://article/62f9357a-4e66-55b8-a23b-3d31e524caf9'}, {'abstract': 'Puerto Ricans are facing the crushing devastation wrought by Hurricane Maria — splintered homes, uprooted trees and floodwaters coursing through streets.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/09/21/us/hurricane-maria-puerto-rico.html', 'snippet': 'Puerto Ricans are facing the crushing devastation wrought by Hurricane Maria — splintered homes, uprooted trees and floodwaters coursing through streets.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Read the latest on Hurricane Maria with Friday’s live updates.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/21/us/21storm-alpha/merlin-t