ublished in the magazine. That is a pretty high bar, though logic might suggest there are some gems among the rejects. At least, that is David Ostow’s theory. He has been submitting his cartoons to the magazine since early last year, but has yet to be published in it.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The New Yorker Said No, but These Cartoons Just May Make Your Day', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Funny, but Not Funny Enough for The New Yorker', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New Yorker', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cartoons and Cartoonists', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-09-21T14:08:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By George Gene Gustines', 'person': [{'firstname': 'George', 'middlename': 'Gene', 'lastname': 'Gustines', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c19a9e60-890f-59c9-98bf-f6d50d52814d', 'word_count': 707, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c19a9e60-890f-59c9-98bf-f6d50d52814d'}, {'abstract': 'For “Festival of Dreams” the Congolese choreographer Faustin Linyekula worked with dancers from It’s Showtime NYC for two weeks.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/09/21/arts/dance/the-center-of-their-own-world.html', 'snippet': 'For “Festival of Dreams” the Congolese choreographer Faustin Linyekula worked with dancers from It’s Showtime NYC for two weeks.', 'lead_paragraph': '', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/20/arts/dance/20INSTAGRAM/20INSTAGRAM-articl