: 'nyt://article/42826318-b821-59e7-a521-3cea7d6f4c98', 'word_count': 1089, 'uri': 'nyt://article/42826318-b821-59e7-a521-3cea7d6f4c98'}, {'abstract': 'For his documentary “The Force,” Peter Nicks tracked the crisis-riddled department for two years.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/09/21/movies/the-force-review-peter-nicks-oakland-police.html', 'snippet': 'For his documentary “The Force,” Peter Nicks tracked the crisis-riddled department for two years.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the potent documentary “The Force,” there’s a moment when Sean Whent, the Oakland chief of police, faces a tough critic: the public. It’s 2015, and he’s talking about the police response to calls. He admits the police are not providing the level of service they should but adds that they’re trying their best. When a robbery victim says their best isn’t good enough, he apologizes. “We need to do a better job, no doubt, and we are trying to do a better job.” By the end of the movie it seems clear that he didn’t apologize enough.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/21/arts/22theforce-web/22theforce-web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/09/21/arts/22theforce-web/22theforce-web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/21/arts/22theforce-web/22theforce-web-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/21/arts/22theforce-web/22theforce-web-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 337, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articl