d.html', 'snippet': 'The killings in Jaghatu District underscore the high casualties Afghan forces are suffering in defending against a resurgent Taliban.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KABUL, Afghanistan — The police chief of a volatile Afghanistan district was killed by a roadside bomb on Thursday, officials said, just two weeks after taking over for his predecessor, who was killed in the same manner.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '3 Police Chiefs Are Killed in a Month in a Volatile Afghan District', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '3 Afghan Police Chiefs  Are Killed in a Month', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Taliban', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ghazni Province (Afghanistan)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-09-21T17:56:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mujib Mashal and Fatima Faizi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mujib', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mashal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Fatima', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Faizi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7b91db3c-77b6-52d5-9ed2-185cc22d7805', 'word_count': 607, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7b91db3c-77b6-52d5-9ed2-185cc22d7805'}, {'abstract': 'We talk about a new startup and why it caused an internet firestorm, and how horror at the movies and on TV reflect our times, in hilarious ways.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/09/21/podcasts/still-processing-outrage-over-bodega-and-horror-at-the-movies.html', 'snippet': 'We talk about a new startup and why it caused an internet firestorm, and how horror at the movies and on TV reflect our times, in hilarious ways.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last week, a Silicon Valley startup called Bodega instigated an internet meltdown after a Fast Company profile made the company’s intentions clear. “Eventually, centralized shopping locations won’t be necessary, because there will be 100,000 Bodegas spread out, with one always 100 feet away from you,” said Paul McDonald, a co-founder, who used to work at Google. The outrage made moral sense. “Bodega” is name that’s asking for trouble, especially with people who frequent them. The outrage is also easy. Where’s the upset over the effect other, bigger companies – like Amazon, whose latest major acquisition, Whole Foods, has slashed prices – might actually have on bodegas? Being mad at Amazon is harder when it’s mixed up in so much of your life. We discuss the dilemma.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/23/insider/21still-processing-1/21still-processing-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/09/23/insider/21still-processing-1/21still-processing-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/23/insider/21still-processing-1/21still-processing-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/23/insider/21still-processing-1/21still-processing-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'cre