e1'}, {'abstract': 'The performance version of Maira Kalman’s book arrives at the Brooklyn Academy of Music.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/09/22/arts/dance/principles-of-uncertainty-bam-maira-kalman.html', 'snippet': 'The performance version of Maira Kalman’s book arrives at the Brooklyn Academy of Music.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On the jacket flap of her 2007 book “The Principles of Uncertainty,” the author and illustrator Maira Kalman briefly explains what the reader will find within — a fragmented personal diary “abounding with anguish, confusion, bits of wisdom, musings, meanderings, buckets of joie de vivre.” Now brought to the stage in collaboration with choreographer John Heginbotham, the performance version of “The Principles of Uncertainty,” arriving Wednesday, Sept. 27, at the Brooklyn Academy of Music, can be described pretty much the same way.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/24/arts/24GUIDE1/24GUIDE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/09/24/arts/24GUIDE1/24GUIDE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/24/arts/24GUIDE1/24GUIDE1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 767, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/24/arts/24GUIDE1/24GUIDE1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1535, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/24/arts/24GUIDE1/24GUIDE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/09/24/arts/24GUIDE1/24GUIDE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/24/arts/24GUIDE1/24GUIDE1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘The Principles of Uncertainty,’ Staged With Joy and Anguish', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Dance; Joy of Life, Right Onstage', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Brooklyn Academy of Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kalman, Maira', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Heginbotham, John', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Principles of Uncertainty (Dance)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-09-22T11:00:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Schaefer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schaefer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/10cbb8da-3315-5025-bfb1-5bc66fbc4e77', 'word_count': 179, 'uri': 'nyt://article/10cbb8da-3315-5025-bfb1-5bc66fbc4e77'}, {'abstract': '“Mary Jane” is a portrait of a mother’s relationship with her chronically ill young son. Carrie Coon of “The Leftovers” stars.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/09/22/theater/amy-herzog-mary-jane.html', 'snippet': '“Mary Jane” is a portrait of a mother’s relationship with her chronically ill young son. Carrie Coon of “The Leftovers” stars.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The director Anne Kauffman has described the playwright Amy Herzog as “an inexhaustible excavator.” Anyone familiar with Ms. Herzog’s work is likely to agree. In plays like “After the Revolution” and “4000 Miles,” Ms. Herzog has dug deep into the terrain where generations intersect, in ways political as well as personal, with a perspective as cleareyed as it is compassionate. Expect the same traits to be in evidence in her latest offering, “Mary Jane,” which opens on Monday, Sept. 25, at the New York Theater Workshop.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/24/arts/24GUIDE2/24GUIDE2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/09/24/arts/24GUIDE2/24GUIDE2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/24/arts/24GUIDE2/24GUIDE2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/24/arts/24GUIDE2/24GUIDE2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/09/24/arts/24GUIDE2/24GUIDE2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 683}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/24/arts/24GUIDE2/24GUIDE2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 900, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/24/arts/24GUIDE2/24GUIDE2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 17