, 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Why Do You Care How Much Other People Work? Revisited', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2017-09-25T07:31:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d8037c3e-38fc-5b9f-be13-7a9a5d0066d8', 'word_count': 263, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d8037c3e-38fc-5b9f-be13-7a9a5d0066d8'}, {'abstract': 'Gianni Berengo Gardin photographed Italy as it hovered between agrarian provincialism and an internationally-touted cosmopolitanism', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2017/09/25/italy-between-past-and-future/', 'snippet': 'Gianni Berengo Gardin photographed Italy as it hovered between agrarian provincialism and an internationally-touted cosmopolitanism', 'lead_paragraph': 'There they are again, the perpetual Italian migrants. They wait on a platform at the Milan train station in 1970, their many suitcases secured with rope, their bags filled to the brim. A box of panettone, a Milanese holiday specialty, accompanies this family of travelers, suggesting Christmastime. Dressed for the cold, the family of five — parents, children, and an older woman wearing black from head to toe — gaze to the right, pondering perhaps their unknown destinies. We see them in Gianni Berengo Gardin’s photograph, shot at mid-distance from above, a portrait of Italy as a migrant nation.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Italy Between Past and Future', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World War II (1939-45)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gardin, Gianni Berengo', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Italy', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-09-25T08:00:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joseph Sciorra', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joseph', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sciorra', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/49368c18-a29a-55d7-a0eb-f0f4d700dd69', 'word_count': 625, 'uri': 'nyt://article/49368c18-a29a-55d7-a0eb-f0f4d700dd69'}, {'abstract': 'Who are the people being targeted by immigration officials seeking to reduce the number of young people being smuggled into the United States?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/09/25/learning/teaching-activities-for-immigration-officials-taking-new-steps-to-discourage-smuggling-of-children.html', 'snippet': 'Who are the people being targeted by immigration officials seeking to reduce the number of young people being smuggled into the United States?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Before reading the article: ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/13/us/13dc-border1/13dc-border1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/09/13/us/13dc-border1/13dc-border1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/13/us/13dc-border1/13dc-border1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumb