ame': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests and Riots', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-09-25T09:54:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Podcasts', 'section_name': 'Podcasts', 'subsection_name': 'The Daily', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Barbaro', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barbaro', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'briefing', '_id': 'nyt://article/73c25c02-c088-5ce6-b5f4-f87a380a17ac', 'word_count': 496, 'uri': 'nyt://article/73c25c02-c088-5ce6-b5f4-f87a380a17ac'}, {'abstract': 'By the time I dropped my daughter off at college, we were both bejeweled with the raised itchy bumps of flea bites.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/09/25/well/family/a-plague-and-a-blessing-in-my-empty-nest.html', 'snippet': 'By the time I dropped my daughter off at college, we were both bejeweled with the raised itchy bumps of flea bites.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A week before I took my only daughter to college in another state this fall, our house became infested with fleas. Combined with the impending sense of child loss, it felt like a biblical plague. Bites accumulated around our ankles and feet, and on me at least, seemed to work their way up further every night toward my neck. By the time I dropped her off, we were both riddled with the raised itchy bumps that we have a shared penchant for scratching raw.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/20/well/family/well-family-fleas/well-family-fleas-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/09/20/well/family/well-family-fleas/well-family-fleas-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge'