 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/25/t-magazine/25tmag-saul-slide-YNPC/25tmag-saul-slide-YNPC-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 850, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/25/t-magazine/25tmag-saul-slide-YNPC/25tmag-saul-slide-YNPC-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1699, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘Saul Leiter’ by François Halard', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2017-09-25T21:06:27+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'T Magazine', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/a94eba80-0166-5f76-9b78-ec1be2366248', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/a94eba80-0166-5f76-9b78-ec1be2366248'}, {'abstract': 'A new photo book documents Saul Leiter’s apartment two years after his death, for a close look at what he left behind.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/09/25/t-magazine/art/saul-leiter-francois-halard.html', 'snippet': 'A new photo book documents Saul Leiter’s apartment two years after his death, for a close look at what he left behind.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Two years after the New York School photographer Saul Leiter died, François Halard had the good fortune to come across the East Village apartment where Leiter lived for more than half a century. Leiter had created some of his best-known work there: gritty scenes of Manhattan streets in the ’50s and ’60s. There was almost nothing left but the barest traces of Leiter’s life — boxes of photographs, a paper lantern, an unfinished sketchbook, a lonely chair — which Halard documents in a new book. In the photographs, taken in 2015, the walls are stained and peeling, the floors spattered with paint. One can clearly see the ravages of time. Yet the soft winter light imbues the rooms with a ghostly beauty and Halard’s haunting images convey the presence of the artist and a lost time.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/25/t-magazine/25tmag-saul-slide-7ZMX/25tmag-saul-slide-7ZMX-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/09/25/t-magazine/25tmag-saul-slide-7ZMX/25tmag-saul-slide-7ZMX-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/25/t-magazine/25tmag-saul-slide-7ZMX/25tmag-saul-slide-7ZMX-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/25/t-magazine/25tmag-saul-slide-7ZMX/25tmag-saul-slide-7ZMX-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 491, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/09/25/t-magazine/25tmag-saul-slide-7ZMX/25tmag-saul-slide-7ZMX-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 491}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/25/t-magazine/25tmag-saul-slide-7ZMX/25tmag-saul-slide-7ZMX-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 838, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/25/t-magazine/25tmag-saul-slide-7ZMX/25tmag-saul-slide-7ZMX-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1676, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Where an Iconic East Village Photographer Lived', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-09-25T21:06:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'subsection_name': 'Art', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tom Delavan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tom', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Delavan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c451c51d-2ccd-5d8c-bd8a-612b4c798dd8', 'word_count': 136, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c451c51d-2ccd-5d8c-bd8a-612b4c798dd8'}, {'abstract': 'Read about how the other side thinks about President Trump’s statements on free speech, the national anthem, the flag as well as responses from football players and owners.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/09/25/us/politics/right-left-nfl-protests-trump.html', 'snippet': 'Read about how the other side thinks about President Trump’s statements on free speech, the national anthem, the flag as well as responses from football players and owners.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The political news cycle is fast, and keeping up can be overwhelming. Trying to find differing perspectives worth your time is even harder. That’s why we have scoured the internet for political writing from the right and left that you might not have seen.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/25/us/25nfl-live-5/25nfl-live-5-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/09/25/us/25nfl-live-5/25nfl-live-5-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption