zation': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e875077d-772d-5c75-8f76-a53e3e23b573', 'word_count': 89, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e875077d-772d-5c75-8f76-a53e3e23b573'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Shepherd, enraged by poaching and other abuses he witnessed while painting wild animals, formed his own conservation foundation.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/09/25/arts/david-shepherd-who-both-painted-and-preserved-wildlife-dies-at-86.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Shepherd, enraged by poaching and other abuses he witnessed while painting wild animals, formed his own conservation foundation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'David Shepherd, a British artist whose love of painting wildlife led him to become a leading conservationist as well, died on Sept. 19 in Sussex, England. He was 86.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/26/obituaries/26shepherd2/25shepherd2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/09/26/obituaries/26shepherd2/25shepherd2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/26/obituaries/26shepherd2/25shepherd2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/26/obituaries/26shepherd2/25shepherd2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 405, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/09/26/obituaries/26shepherd2/25shepherd2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 405}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/26/obituaries/26shepherd2/25shepherd2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 692, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/26/obituaries/26shepherd2/25shepherd2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1383, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'David Shepherd, Who Both Painted and Preserved Wildlife, Dies at 86', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'David Shepherd, 86, a Leading Advocate For the Wildlife That He Loved to Paint', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shepherd, David (1931-2017)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ANIMALS', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Conservation of Resources', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-09-25T21:59:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Obits', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Neil Genzlinger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Neil', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Genzlinger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/5d4590fc-a349-5156-9646-0c395f7c9149', 'word_count': 893, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5d4590fc-a349-5156-9646-0c395f7c9149'}, {'abstract': 'The president and the league he is criticizing have a lot in common.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/09/25/magazine/before-trump-brought-politics-into-football-he-made-politics-into-football.html', 'snippet': 'The president and the league he is criticizing have a lot in common.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When all else fails, the National Football League has always been able to market its product as an escape — from all that. Football provides fans “a chance to really celebrate and come together and get away from our everyday troubles,” Commissioner Roger Goodell said in an interview with CBS’s Bob Schieffer before the Super Bowl in 2010. Yes, life is hard, full of “troubles,” but Sundays offer the solace of a beginning-to-end emotional experience. Games are confined to about three hours and yield unambiguous, stick-to-sports results. “We offer a respite,” the Dallas Cowboys owner Jerry Jones told me in 2016. “We are a respite that moves you away from your trials and missteps, or my trials and missteps.”', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/25/magazine/25mag-nfl1/25mag-nfl1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 432, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/09/25/magazine/25mag-nfl1/25mag-nfl1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 432}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/25/magazine/25mag-nfl1/25mag-nfl1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 737, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/25/magazine/25mag-nfl1/25mag-nfl1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1475, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/25/magazine/25mag-nfl1/25mag-nfl1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/09/25/magazine/25mag-nfl1/25mag-nfl1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 7