evelop in the region, then spread elsewhere. Eliminating it there will require all the weapons we have.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/09/26/opinion/fighting-malaria-mekong.html', 'snippet': 'Drug-resistant malaria strains often develop in the region, then spread elsewhere. Eliminating it there will require all the weapons we have.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Malaria infected more than 200 million people in 2015, and killed more than 400,000, most of them children in Africa. As devastating as those numbers are, they were a major improvement: Deaths  fell by  48 percent since 2000. This impressive drop was the result of billions in funding and decades of effort by thousands of people across the globe.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/26/opinion/26ploweWeb/26ploweWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/09/26/opinion/26ploweWeb/26ploweWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/26/opinion/26ploweWeb/26ploweWeb-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/26/opinion/26ploweWeb/26ploweWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 404, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/09/26/opinion/26ploweWeb/26ploweWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 404}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/26/opinion/26ploweWeb/26ploweWeb-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 690, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/26/opinion/26ploweWeb/26ploweWeb-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1379, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Taking the Battle Against Malaria to the Mekong', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Malaria', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Gates, Bill and Melinda, Foundation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "President's Malaria Initiative", 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'World Health Organization', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Vietnam', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cambodia', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Laos', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mekong River', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Myanmar', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Thailand', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-09-26T07:21:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christopher Plowe', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christopher', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Plowe', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/19e375f5-118d-5fa2-a509-5bce40e62f53', 'word_count': 1142, 'uri': 'nyt://article/19e375f5-118d-5fa2-a509-5bce40e62f53'}, {'abstract': 'Yes, but only when it’s an excuse to cut social spending. Tax cuts — now that’s a different story.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/09/26/opinion/do-republicans-really-care-about-the-deficit.html', 'snippet': 'Yes, but only when it’s an excuse to cut social spending. Tax cuts — now that’s a different story.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Though America really doesn’t need a tax cut — demographic pressures alone suggest the need for more, not less, future revenues — President Trump and the Republican majority want one. But they don’t want to pay for it, which means the budget deficit is going to rise. Based on what we’ve seen so far, the increase in the deficit could be at least $1.5 trillion over 10 years.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/26/opinion/26bernsteinWeb/26bernsteinWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/09/26/opinion/26bernsteinWeb/26bernsteinWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/26/opinion/26bernsteinWeb/26bernsteinWeb-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/26/opinion/26bernsteinWeb/26bernsteinWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 410, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/09/26/opinion/26bernsteinWeb/26bernsteinWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 410}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/26/opinion/26bernsteinWeb/26bernsteinWeb-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 699, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/26/opinion/26bernsteinWeb/26bernsteinWeb-superJumb