ame': 'Thomas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 3}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/8fdff4b8-73e4-56ac-8e95-52c5d6573e9d', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/8fdff4b8-73e4-56ac-8e95-52c5d6573e9d'}, {'abstract': 'When, at 94, she suddenly found it difficult to speak and swallow, the doctors had to explore more unusual possibilities.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/09/26/magazine/all-signs-pointed-to-a-stroke-then-the-tests-come-back-negative.html', 'snippet': 'When, at 94, she suddenly found it difficult to speak and swallow, the doctors had to explore more unusual possibilities.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Mom?” the middle-aged man asked. He recognized the voice, but the words were muffled and strange. I’ll be right over, he said into the phone. The 15-minute drive from his small Connecticut town to his mother’s seemed to last forever. Had she had a stroke? She was 94, and though she’d always been healthy, at her age, anything could happen.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/01/magazine/01diagnosis1/01diagnosis1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/10/01/magazine/01diagnosis1/01diagnosis1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/01/magazine/01diagnosis1/01diagnosis1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/01/magazine/01diagnosis1/01mag-01diagnosis-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 550, 'width': 600