de a comeback. If the recent flood of ’90s-based true-crime TV is any indication, we clearly feel some similar nostalgia toward even violent crime. It’s a little bit twisted (guilty), and the reason is anybody’s guess (Dr. Freud?), but it’s no less true for its strangeness: ’90s crime is as much a part of the zeitgeist as chokers and emo-band reunions.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/26/watching/26lawandwatching-02/26lawandwatching-02-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/09/26/watching/26lawandwatching-02/26lawandwatching-02-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/26/watching/26lawandwatching-02/26lawandwatching-02-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/26/watching/26lawandwatching-02/26lawandwatching-02-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/09/26/watching/26lawandwatching-02/26lawandwatching-02-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/26/watching/26lawandwatching-02/26lawandwatching-02-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/26/watching/26lawandwatching-02/26lawandwatching-02-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJ