': 'Southeast Asia Stakes Its Claim in the Art World', 'kicker': 'Art Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Stepping Out From History', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Asia Society', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'After Darkness: Southeast Asian Art in the Wake of History (Exhibit)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vietnam War', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Political Prisoners', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Le, Dinh Q', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Propeller Group', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-09-27T15:00:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jason Farago', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jason', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Farago', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/d02538b8-76d0-5945-947f-fb923776c34c', 'word_count': 1296, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d02538b8-76d0-5945-947f-fb923776c34c'}, {'abstract': 'NBC’s family dramedy has been beating a dead character for too long, and the contrived mystery is getting distracting.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/09/27/arts/television/this-is-us-jack.html', 'snippet': 'NBC’s family dramedy has been beating a dead character for too long, and the contrived mystery is getting distracting.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On the season premiere of NBC’s “This Is Us,” we finally got clarity on a nagging question. In a flashback to just after the death of Jack (Milo Ventimiglia), his distraught wife, Rebecca (Mandy Moore), pulled up, crying, in front of the flame-gutted shell of their house. So this was the answer: Jac