: 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/09/29/arts/music/walt-whitman-leaves-of-grass-opera-crossing-aucoin.html', 'snippet': 'One of America’s greatest writers spent his formative years idolizing divas and listening to Italian operas.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Walt Whitman wasn’t always an opera fan. As a budding young journalist in New York, he was known to take potshots at the etiquette and artifice of what he saw as an aristocratic pastime. Whitman cultivated a more democratic persona and preferred popular songs, which he called “heart” — as opposed to “art” — music.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/01/arts/01WHITMAN1/01WHITMAN1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/10/01/arts/01WHITMAN1/01WHITMAN1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/01/arts/01WHITMAN1/01WHITMAN1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/01/arts/01WHITMAN1/01WHITMAN1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 598, 'width': 438, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/01/arts/01WHITMAN1/01WHITMAN1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 598, 'width': 438, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'How Opera Inspired Walt Whitman’s ‘Leaves of Grass’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In ‘Leaves of the Grass,’ an Ode to Opera', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Whitman, Walt', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Opera', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poetry and Poets', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Crossing (Opera)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Aucoin, Matthew (1990- )', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-09-29T14:00:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joshua Barone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joshua', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8cbf17c1-416c-5372-9289-70b3eef39f4e', 'word_count': 1457, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8cbf17c1-416c-5372-9289-70b3eef39f4e'}, {'abstract': 'Ms. Acogny, a driving force in contemporary African dance, will be at the Brooklyn Academy of Music in “Mon Élue Noire” (“My Black Chosen One”).', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/09/29/arts/dance/germaine-acogny-mon-elue-noire-bam.html', 'snippet': 'Ms. Acogny, a driving force in contemporary African dance, will be at the Brooklyn Academy of Music in “Mon Élue Noire” (“My Black Chosen One”).', 'lead_paragraph': 'Germaine Acogny was first chosen some 40 years ago. She was then the director of Mudra Afrique, the most prestigious school of dance in her country, Senegal. One day, Maurice Béjart, the prominent French choreographer who had founded the school, announced that he wanted her African students to perform his erotic version of Stravinsky’s “The Rite of Spring.” And who would play the woman selected for the climactic mating ritual? “You will be my black chosen one,” Béjart told her.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/01/arts/01ACOGNY1/01ACOGNY1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/10/01/arts/01ACOGNY1/01ACOGNY1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/01/arts/01ACOGNY1/01ACOGNY1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/01/arts/01ACOGNY1/01ACOGNY1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 1124, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/10/01/arts/01ACOGNY1/01ACOGNY1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 1124}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/01/arts/01ACOGNY1/01ACOGNY1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 547, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/01/arts/01ACOGNY1/01ACOGNY1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1093, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Germaine Acogny on Choosing to Be the Chosen One', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Choosing to Be the Chosen One', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Brooklyn Academy of Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Acogny, Germaine', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Mon Elue Noire (Dance)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-09-29T14:00:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Seibert', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Seibert', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f26eb379-e548-5cc3-b761-4523e8833448', 'word_count': 1267, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f26eb379-e548-5cc3-b761-4523e8833448'}, {'abstract': 'The secretary of state is to arrive in Beijing to discuss North Korea. Chinese officials are likely to see if he can clarify inconsistent statements made by U.S. officials.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/09/29/world/asia/rex-tillerson-china-north-korea.html', 'snippet': 'The secretary of state is to arrive in Beijing to discuss North Korea. Chinese officials are likely to see if he can clarify inconsistent statements made by U.S. officials.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIJING — Secretary of State Rex W. Tillerson is scheduled to arrive in Beijing early Saturday for a brief visit, amid confusing signals about President Trump’s position on two questions looming over the confrontation with North Korea: Is America’s long-term goal to overthrow its leader, Kim Jong-un, or just try to change his behavior? And what would it take to get negotiations with Pyongyang started?', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/30/world/30NKOREA1/30NKOREA1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/09/30/world/30NKOREA1/30NKOREA1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 