whole or at least the right side of the political spectrum as a pure oligarchy, where the big money controls everything. And money definitely plays an outsized and generally malign role in policy. Usually, however, it’s only the root of some evil, not all evil: the vileness of a Roy Moore or Joe Arpaio comes from very different sources,', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Unpopular Delusions and the Madness of Elites', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2017-09-29T16:55:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/db44c5e1-0536-506d-b876-95d935957e10', 'word_count': 189, 'uri': 'nyt://article/db44c5e1-0536-506d-b876-95d935957e10'}, {'abstract': 'Our weekly look for and about Canadians reviews the latest trade tussle between Canada and the United States and previews a Broadway show with Canadian input.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/09/29/world/canada/canada-letter-nafta-trade.html', 'snippet': 'Our weekly look for and about Canadians reviews the latest trade tussle between Canada and the United States and previews a Broadway show with Canadian input.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This week the roadshow to renegotiate the North American Free Trade Agreement made its way to Ottawa. Although the city was suffering through an exceptional September heat wave, the Canadian government offered school buses that lacked air conditioning to shuttle government officials and reporters to and from the site hosting the talks.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/29/world/30canadaletter-nafta/30canadaletter-nafta-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 379, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/09/29/world/30canadaletter-nafta/30canadaletter-nafta-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 379}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/29/world/30canadaletter-nafta/30canadaletter-nafta-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 647, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/29/world/30canadaletter-nafta/30canadaletter-nafta-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1294, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/29/world/30canadaletter-nafta/30canadaletter-nafta-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/09/29/world/30canadaletter-nafta/30canadaletter-nafta-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/29/world/30canadaletter-nafta/30canadaletter-nafta-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Canada Letter: The Land Where Trade Talks Make Headlines', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'North American Free Trade Agreement', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Canada', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-09-29T16:56:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Canada', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ian Austen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Austen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4ccd68f6-996b-5149-815f-52df8d7e750a', 'word_count': 952, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4ccd68f6-996b-5149-815f-52df8d7e750a'}, {'abstract': 'I was fighting for women’s liberation. The Playboy creator only pretended to.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/09/29/opinion/sunday/hugh-hefner.html', 'snippet': 'I was fighting for women’s liberation. The Playboy creator only pretended to.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On March 26, 1970, I accepted an invitation to appear on “The Dick Cavett Show” to talk about a new movement I was involved with called Women’s Liberation. I knew that our young movement was suspicious of activists who sought media attention, so I roped my friend Sally Kempton, a talented writer, into coming with me. I don’t recall if we knew ahead of time who the principal guest that evening would be. He turned out to be Hugh Hefner.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/29/opinion/29brownmillerWeb/29brownmillerWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 530, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/09/29/opinion/29brownmillerWeb/29brownmillerWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 530}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/29/opinion/29brownmillerWeb/29brownmillerWeb-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 904, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/29/opinion/29brownmillerWeb/29brownmillerWeb-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1808, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/29/opinion/29brownmillerWeb/29brownmillerWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/09/29/opinion/29brownmillerWeb/29brownmillerWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/29/opinion/29brownmillerWeb/29brownmillerWeb-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Hugh Hefner Was My Enemy', 'kicker': 'Opinion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Hugh Hefner Was My Enemy', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hefner, Hugh', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': "Women's Rights", 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Playboy Magazine', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Playboy Foundation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cavett, Dick', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-09-29T16:56:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Susan Brownmiller', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Susan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brownmiller', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/ac07a1bd-b2a7-59f8-b156-4354529d6b4b', 'word_count': 841, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ac07a1bd-b2a7-59f8-b156-4354529d6b4b'}, {'abstract': 'A chocolate chip cookie, thin with crisp ripples that run to the edges, finds Instagram fame.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/09/29/dining/chocolate-chip-cookie-recipe-instagram.html', 'snippet': 'A chocolate chip cookie, thin with crisp ripples that run to the edges, finds Instagram fame.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last fall, an aberrant chocolate chip cookie turned up in my Instagram feed. As wide as a salad plate and flat as a flounder, it appeared thin, but it was somehow layered with slabs of chocolate. Oddest of all, it was ringed, like a tree trunk — as if a chunk of chocolate had been dropped in the center and somehow made waves out to the edges. I assumed it was a mutant, posted by a troubled baker as a cry for help, and I kept scrolling.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/04/dining/04Cookie/04Cookie-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/10/04/dining/04Cookie/04Cookie-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/04/dining/04Cookie/04Cookie-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/04/dining/04Cookie/04Cookie-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/04/dining/04Cookie/04Cookie-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images